WEBVTT

1
00:00:13,416 --> 00:00:17,125
{\an8}[radio host over radio] <i>Turn it up.</i>
<i>Turn it up!</i>

2
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:21,541
{\an8}[man over radio] <i>What's up, y'all?</i>
<i>This is Paulo Brown, voice of the favela.</i>

3
00:00:21,625 --> 00:00:22,875
<i>Keeping the good vibes coming,</i>

4
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:26,666
<i>because every step you take</i>
<i>is a step closer to the dream.</i>

5
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,458
<i>And you're almost there.</i>

6
00:00:28,541 --> 00:00:30,916
["Forte Pra Dar Sorte"
by MC Hariel playing]

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,958
[brakes screeching]

8
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:34,208
[whirring]

9
00:00:34,958 --> 00:00:36,166
[squeaking]

10
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:38,208
-[inaudible]
-[dogs barking]

11
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:40,541
[indistinct chatter]

12
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,583
[buzzing]

13
00:00:43,666 --> 00:00:44,833
[whirring]

14
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:48,041
[flapping]

15
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:48,958
[revving]

16
00:00:49,041 --> 00:00:50,250
[inaudible]

17
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,375
[whirring]

18
00:00:52,541 --> 00:00:53,458
[meows]

19
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,625
[bird chirping]

20
00:00:55,708 --> 00:00:57,000
[revving]

21
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:05,875
[song fades]

22
00:01:05,958 --> 00:01:07,958
[woman] Yeah, that view
never gets old, does it?

23
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:10,291
-The only thing getting old is us.
-[woman chuckles]

24
00:01:10,375 --> 00:01:12,250
If you knew what I go through
at that office…

25
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:14,125
Sometimes I don't even have time
to breathe.

26
00:01:14,208 --> 00:01:16,041
[man] Imagine
when you get your own office.

27
00:01:16,125 --> 00:01:17,708
-God willing! [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

28
00:01:17,791 --> 00:01:20,625
Gimme a few years, I'll get there.
Baby steps though, huh?

29
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,375
How's the record label coming along?

30
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,833
Oh, I'm tryna live more purposeful
these days.

31
00:01:25,916 --> 00:01:27,958
I have the church stuff,
and Chiquinho on the side.

32
00:01:28,041 --> 00:01:30,791
-Kid's more than enough work. [chuckles]
-Adulting, huh?

33
00:01:32,083 --> 00:01:33,416
Have you two been talking?

34
00:01:34,791 --> 00:01:36,666
Eh, barely. Have you?

35
00:01:37,583 --> 00:01:39,083
Nah, not really.

36
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:42,333
I hear more about him than from him.
Scheyla fills me in.

37
00:01:42,416 --> 00:01:44,500
He hasn't seen the kids in a long time.

38
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,541
She says Nando's not himself these days.

39
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:50,250
I miss it being the three of us.
All together.

40
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:52,166
[pensive music playing]

41
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,333
Same here.

42
00:01:55,625 --> 00:01:56,791
But he's out there.

43
00:01:57,625 --> 00:01:58,541
On top of the world.

44
00:01:58,625 --> 00:02:01,250
With more responsibilities
and more problems.

45
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:04,250
Where he's at, I doubt
he'll ever come back to Brazil.

46
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:07,041
["Balkanika" by Relativ playing]

47
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:09,958
[helicopter blades whirring]

48
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,458
{\an8}BELGRADE - SERBIA

49
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:35,875
[in Serbian] Inbound for landing.

50
00:02:51,666 --> 00:02:53,500
[man, in English] Ah, there he is!

51
00:02:54,625 --> 00:02:55,791
Hey, brother.

52
00:02:55,875 --> 00:02:57,750
-You good? Good to see you.
-Yeah, all good.

53
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:18,375
[song ends]

54
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:19,375
BALKAN HOTEL

55
00:03:20,708 --> 00:03:22,708
[indistinct chatter]

56
00:03:23,958 --> 00:03:25,375
[motorcycle revving]

57
00:03:27,666 --> 00:03:28,750
Moicano.

58
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:30,750
Same deal, got me?

59
00:03:31,291 --> 00:03:33,000
I got your back, ND.

60
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:34,791
[sirens wailing in distance]

61
00:03:39,291 --> 00:03:41,833
[club bass pounding in distance]

62
00:03:41,916 --> 00:03:44,083
[indistinct chatter]

63
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:53,708
["Hocu Sve" by Krtina
playing over speakers]

64
00:03:55,875 --> 00:03:57,958
[indistinct chatter, cheering]

65
00:04:13,958 --> 00:04:16,833
-[song continues in distance]
-[indistinct chatter]

66
00:04:16,916 --> 00:04:18,166
Okay, wait here.

67
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,208
If things get loud, you come in.

68
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:22,916
ND, long time.

69
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Sascha. Bojan.

70
00:04:25,083 --> 00:04:27,333
-[exhales]
-[ND] This is Paulo.

71
00:04:27,416 --> 00:04:29,083
Our partner from accounts.

72
00:04:29,166 --> 00:04:32,583
So he take care of the numbers.
And you take care of us.

73
00:04:32,666 --> 00:04:33,958
[ND] That's right.

74
00:04:35,958 --> 00:04:38,000
Okay. Fill me in then.

75
00:04:38,083 --> 00:04:41,875
We were just saying
that the last shipment you sent

76
00:04:41,958 --> 00:04:43,583
was a success.

77
00:04:44,166 --> 00:04:47,958
We make the Japanese, Chinese, Australian,
everybody happy.

78
00:04:48,041 --> 00:04:50,416
And so this time we want double.

79
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,666
With same split.

80
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:54,833
Fifty percent before delivery,
fifty percent after delivery.

81
00:04:55,416 --> 00:04:58,625
Divided between the crypto,
weapons, real estate, and soccer.

82
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:01,333
Which Brazilians love just as much as us.

83
00:05:01,416 --> 00:05:02,916
The best deal's a finished deal.

84
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,541
And while we're at it, why don't we settle
the shortfall from the last shipment.

85
00:05:07,125 --> 00:05:09,208
[chuckles] Shortfall?

86
00:05:09,291 --> 00:05:10,791
[tense music playing]

87
00:05:11,583 --> 00:05:12,833
Adding up

88
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,125
the money and the assets…

89
00:05:18,541 --> 00:05:21,208
you're about two million short
from the last shipment.

90
00:05:33,541 --> 00:05:36,041
[in Serbian] They say
we didn't pay in full.

91
00:05:42,416 --> 00:05:45,333
[in English] All the transfers
and contributions was made.

92
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:47,666
The numbers don't lie, bro.

93
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:49,000
What are you saying?

94
00:05:49,666 --> 00:05:51,166
My brother's a liar?

95
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:54,833
We're not here to cause problems, guys.
We're here to make a deal.

96
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:57,708
With interest.

97
00:05:58,958 --> 00:06:01,833
Now you want us to make receipt
for taxes we owe you, man?

98
00:06:01,916 --> 00:06:04,875
Or how about your word is my receipt, man?

99
00:06:04,958 --> 00:06:06,916
[in Serbian] Maybe
you got the numbers wrong.

100
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,625
Or you lied to your brother.

101
00:06:09,791 --> 00:06:12,250
[in English] Between you
and my own brother,

102
00:06:12,333 --> 00:06:14,041
I trust my brother.

103
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:17,625
You should know, man.
Everyone's a brother in the favela.

104
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:19,166
But not here.

105
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,416
Here, brother is flesh.

106
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,833
First, we'll settle the shortfall
from the last time.

107
00:06:25,916 --> 00:06:27,250
[inhales, exhales]

108
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:29,208
Then we can talk about the next shipment.

109
00:06:31,625 --> 00:06:33,416
[in Serbian] They're blackmailing us.

110
00:06:34,208 --> 00:06:37,041
They want more money,
or they'll stop selling.

111
00:06:37,125 --> 00:06:39,875
But we do business with or without them.

112
00:06:44,958 --> 00:06:46,500
[in English] All right, here's the deal.

113
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,583
You apologize to us.
And you make new delivery.

114
00:06:53,625 --> 00:06:55,833
Or we will find a new partner.

115
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:59,750
Didn't you live with your uncle in Brazil?

116
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:04,166
Petar Ilic.

117
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:05,541
[laughs]

118
00:07:05,625 --> 00:07:06,833
[ND] Nice name.

119
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:09,916
Three years.

120
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,291
Let me tell you something
that Petar clearly didn't.

121
00:07:13,375 --> 00:07:17,125
Ninety five percent of the blow
that makes its way through Europe

122
00:07:17,208 --> 00:07:18,583
I bring here.

123
00:07:18,666 --> 00:07:20,166
Without us, you two have no business.

124
00:07:20,250 --> 00:07:21,083
[dramatic sting]

125
00:07:22,458 --> 00:07:24,041
You think you're back in Brazil, huh?

126
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:26,208
[club music playing]

127
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:30,083
[club music continues in distance]

128
00:07:30,166 --> 00:07:31,041
[tense music playing]

129
00:07:31,875 --> 00:07:33,208
-[gunshot]
-[Moicano grunts]

130
00:07:33,291 --> 00:07:35,541
-[gunshots]
-[indistinct shouts]

131
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,708
[ND] Get down! Get down, fuck!

132
00:07:58,166 --> 00:07:59,625
[gunshots stop]

133
00:07:59,708 --> 00:08:02,166
[tense music continues]

134
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:04,625
-[screaming]
-[gunshots]

135
00:08:04,708 --> 00:08:05,875
[gun clicks]

136
00:08:05,958 --> 00:08:07,250
[Sasha grunts]

137
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:09,125
[suspenseful music playing]

138
00:08:09,875 --> 00:08:11,708
[inhales, exhales]

139
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,416
[ND] Did you really think
you were gonna kill me?

140
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:26,458
I've been to the other side, man.

141
00:08:28,125 --> 00:08:29,791
And I won't be going back.

142
00:08:34,375 --> 00:08:35,208
Let's head out.

143
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:40,041
[indistinct chatter]

144
00:08:40,125 --> 00:08:42,166
Do you know what you just did?

145
00:08:42,250 --> 00:08:44,541
Who the fuck gave you the go-ahead
to do that?

146
00:08:44,625 --> 00:08:46,458
They were trying to kill us, ND.

147
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:48,750
[intriguing music playing]

148
00:08:54,125 --> 00:08:58,000
{\an8}NANDO BETWEEN TWO WORLDS
- A SINTONIA FILM

149
00:08:58,791 --> 00:09:00,125
[music fades]

150
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:02,916
-[woman] Happy Father's Day!
-[crowd cheering]

151
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:08,250
Hey!

152
00:09:08,958 --> 00:09:11,083
Yeah! Enzo! [kiss]

153
00:09:14,625 --> 00:09:17,291
["Se Essa Rua" by Mc Vitória playing]

154
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,166
[chuckles]

155
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:46,125
[chuckles]

156
00:09:46,208 --> 00:09:47,500
[boy] I had it at home.

157
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,875
Sorry?

158
00:09:49,458 --> 00:09:51,125
I had it. I had it at home.

159
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:53,041
Ah. [chuckles]

160
00:09:53,125 --> 00:09:55,250
Too bad I wasn't there
to see you prove it.

161
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:56,875
Hm. How's tonight?

162
00:09:58,916 --> 00:10:01,666
No, I can't. I have a dinner thing
with my family later.

163
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:04,500
Hmm… You're celebrating Father's Day?

164
00:10:05,458 --> 00:10:07,750
No, it's just dinner with my grandma.

165
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:12,250
We're the only ones
not celebrating the holiday, I guess. Hmm?

166
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,375
Yeah. But let's hang another time.

167
00:10:15,458 --> 00:10:16,958
[boy] I don't know what's worse.

168
00:10:18,958 --> 00:10:20,708
Having a dad that died or…

169
00:10:21,291 --> 00:10:23,458
or one who disappeared, like mine.

170
00:10:23,541 --> 00:10:24,958
[skateboard rolling away]

171
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,750
[pensive music playing]

172
00:10:28,416 --> 00:10:29,541
[engine idling]

173
00:10:29,625 --> 00:10:31,375
[ND] You know how it goes, man.

174
00:10:31,958 --> 00:10:34,333
Those guys were already on us, you know?

175
00:10:34,416 --> 00:10:38,000
So when the one guy pulled his gun,
Moicano drew his straight away, man.

176
00:10:38,083 --> 00:10:39,875
And you know the rest, brother.

177
00:10:39,958 --> 00:10:41,750
If you draw, you have to shoot,
no other way.

178
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:43,500
[man over phone] <i>Fuck, bro.</i>

179
00:10:43,583 --> 00:10:46,000
<i>These guys</i>
<i>have been our partners for years.</i>

180
00:10:46,083 --> 00:10:48,875
We need to fix this,
clean up this mess, ND.

181
00:10:48,958 --> 00:10:50,625
[ND] <i>I'm out of here, man.</i>

182
00:10:50,708 --> 00:10:52,291
Going straight to Bosnia.

183
00:10:52,375 --> 00:10:53,958
After that, Italy.

184
00:10:54,541 --> 00:10:57,666
Soon as I'm in a safe spot,
I'm gonna sort this out with them myself.

185
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:01,000
You're aware that Petar Ilic
isn't just the Serbians' boss, right?

186
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:02,541
He's also their uncle.

187
00:11:02,625 --> 00:11:04,750
<i>He'll want payback.</i>

188
00:11:04,833 --> 00:11:05,875
Brother,

189
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,750
I just wanted to ask you
to look out for my family.

190
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:13,458
<i>Until I can prove</i>
<i>that those rats started this whole thing.</i>

191
00:11:13,541 --> 00:11:15,208
<i>You're well aware that for the Serbians,</i>

192
00:11:15,291 --> 00:11:17,666
<i>blood can only be paid for</i>
<i>with more blood.</i>

193
00:11:18,708 --> 00:11:20,708
Don't you worry, ND.

194
00:11:20,791 --> 00:11:22,375
We'll step up our security.

195
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:23,916
<i>As long as you're gone,</i>

196
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,208
<i>no one's gonna fuck</i>
<i>with your family, okay?</i>

197
00:11:26,291 --> 00:11:27,208
Hm.

198
00:11:27,875 --> 00:11:28,791
[vibrating]

199
00:11:28,875 --> 00:11:30,666
INCOMING VIDEO CALL
SCHEYLA

200
00:11:31,791 --> 00:11:32,916
[ND] Okay.

201
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,208
I'm outta here, Joel.

202
00:11:35,541 --> 00:11:36,916
We're in this together.

203
00:11:37,541 --> 00:11:39,583
Thank you. Talk soon.

204
00:11:41,291 --> 00:11:43,083
[woman] Enzo, talk to Daddy.

205
00:11:43,166 --> 00:11:44,000
[game chiming]

206
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:45,708
Happy Father's Day.

207
00:11:45,791 --> 00:11:46,833
[chuckles]

208
00:11:46,916 --> 00:11:48,833
Thank you, my Enzo.

209
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,791
How did the performance go at school?

210
00:11:50,875 --> 00:11:53,791
Good. Grandma and Mommy really liked it.

211
00:11:53,875 --> 00:11:55,458
Kinda sucks you weren't there though.

212
00:11:56,125 --> 00:11:58,791
But your papa was there in spirit
with you guys, okay?

213
00:11:58,875 --> 00:12:00,416
<i>Did your mom record it?</i>

214
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:02,958
<i>Tell her to send it to me.</i>
<i>I want to see it, okay?</i>

215
00:12:04,083 --> 00:12:07,291
<i>How are things going over there, bud?</i>
<i>School, karate…</i>

216
00:12:07,375 --> 00:12:09,833
The same. Not much has changed.

217
00:12:09,916 --> 00:12:10,833
[ND] <i>The same?</i>

218
00:12:10,916 --> 00:12:12,125
That's it?

219
00:12:13,458 --> 00:12:16,208
<i>Your sister hasn't called</i>
<i>to wish me happy Father's Day.</i>

220
00:12:16,291 --> 00:12:17,666
<i>Where is she?</i>

221
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:19,291
She's outside with Grandma.

222
00:12:21,208 --> 00:12:23,625
Grandma, do you really think
my mom would let me?

223
00:12:23,708 --> 00:12:25,375
-No way.
-[chuckles]

224
00:12:25,458 --> 00:12:26,291
[Grandma laughs]

225
00:12:26,375 --> 00:12:28,625
-And neither will I, actually.
-[laughs]

226
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,333
Oh, it's bad enough

227
00:12:31,416 --> 00:12:34,583
that your mother dated boys at school
without me knowing.

228
00:12:34,666 --> 00:12:36,125
But I'm not like my mom.

229
00:12:36,208 --> 00:12:38,666
And besides,
I have brought up Murilo a few times.

230
00:12:38,750 --> 00:12:40,250
I know, honey.

231
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:44,583
But you're so young,
so much life ahead of you.

232
00:12:44,666 --> 00:12:48,375
Is it too much to ask
for you to pump the brakes on this thing?

233
00:12:52,583 --> 00:12:53,958
How about we do this…

234
00:12:54,041 --> 00:12:59,000
Invite Murilo to the square one day,
so I can get to meet him.

235
00:12:59,083 --> 00:13:00,625
Oh. I like that.

236
00:13:00,708 --> 00:13:01,750
Mm.

237
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:02,708
Then we'll see.

238
00:13:02,791 --> 00:13:05,666
[chuckling] Okay.

239
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,833
[cell phone ringing, vibrating]

240
00:13:09,166 --> 00:13:11,083
INCOMING CALL
DAD

241
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,208
Answer your father, my love.

242
00:13:14,291 --> 00:13:16,500
[cell phone continues ringing, vibrating]

243
00:13:16,583 --> 00:13:18,583
[pensive music playing]

244
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:22,625
[sighs]

245
00:13:23,416 --> 00:13:24,875
I… It's just…

246
00:13:26,625 --> 00:13:29,083
I don't have any more to say to him,
you know what I mean?

247
00:13:30,083 --> 00:13:31,416
Tell you dad about Murilo.

248
00:13:32,458 --> 00:13:34,166
Tell him about your life.

249
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:38,208
You haven't seen each other face to face
for nearly two years, give or take.

250
00:13:38,291 --> 00:13:39,125
I know that.

251
00:13:39,916 --> 00:13:43,708
It just feels like every time we do,
we end up fighting about something.

252
00:13:45,333 --> 00:13:47,958
Anyway, why are you suddenly
sticking up for my dad?

253
00:13:48,666 --> 00:13:50,791
Because he's still your dad.

254
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,208
My dad is dead.

255
00:14:03,416 --> 00:14:04,541
[glass shatters]

256
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:08,041
What's the matter?

257
00:14:08,125 --> 00:14:10,500
Nothing. Everything's fine.

258
00:14:11,083 --> 00:14:14,416
["Remix Herói ou Vilão (Uma série Netflix
'Sintonia - Temporada 5'")

259
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,625
by MC Jottapê playing]

260
00:14:45,458 --> 00:14:46,875
[birds chirping]

261
00:14:46,958 --> 00:14:48,708
[song fades]

262
00:14:54,166 --> 00:14:58,000
That was the first and last time
I put numbers before business, ND.

263
00:14:59,458 --> 00:15:01,416
They almost cut off my hand, bro.

264
00:15:04,416 --> 00:15:06,916
You can't underestimate
these guys, brother.

265
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,833
Yeah, but they're not going
for your hand anymore.

266
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,333
Now they're aiming for my head.

267
00:15:12,416 --> 00:15:14,291
[tense music playing]

268
00:15:14,375 --> 00:15:16,041
[cell phone chimes]

269
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,750
[ND] They're at my place.

270
00:15:24,208 --> 00:15:26,125
We gotta do something, man.

271
00:15:26,916 --> 00:15:28,791
These guys won't stop until we do.

272
00:15:35,958 --> 00:15:38,083
[cell phone chiming]

273
00:15:40,958 --> 00:15:42,375
You good, bro?

274
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:45,750
It's just my family, man.

275
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:46,958
Damn…

276
00:15:48,041 --> 00:15:50,166
That's why I never got married, bro.

277
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:52,458
Nothing more messy than family, you know?

278
00:15:53,666 --> 00:15:56,041
Putting down roots only slows you down.

279
00:15:58,458 --> 00:16:00,208
Guys like the two of us

280
00:16:01,458 --> 00:16:02,958
have way bigger responsibilities.

281
00:16:11,291 --> 00:16:12,375
INSPECTION POINT

282
00:16:12,458 --> 00:16:14,125
[police officer] Papers, please.

283
00:16:19,166 --> 00:16:20,708
Glasses off.

284
00:16:20,791 --> 00:16:23,000
INSPECTION AREA

285
00:16:26,125 --> 00:16:28,000
[tense music continues]

286
00:16:37,416 --> 00:16:38,708
All right. Good to go.

287
00:16:42,541 --> 00:16:44,208
[sheep bleating]

288
00:16:44,291 --> 00:16:46,208
[cowbell clanking]

289
00:16:47,041 --> 00:16:50,500
-[helicopter blades whirring]
-[sirens wailing in distance]

290
00:16:54,875 --> 00:16:56,791
[tires screeching]

291
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:02,833
[engine shuts off]

292
00:17:06,583 --> 00:17:08,250
[intriguing music playing]

293
00:17:09,083 --> 00:17:11,166
[man, in Serbian] We were too late.

294
00:17:11,666 --> 00:17:14,208
The Brazilian's house was empty.

295
00:17:14,291 --> 00:17:17,791
He could have left Serbia by now.

296
00:17:17,875 --> 00:17:23,916
But he still has strong ties here,
in Brazil.

297
00:17:29,458 --> 00:17:31,416
[menacing music playing]

298
00:17:32,708 --> 00:17:34,041
[objects cluttering]

299
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:35,458
-[gasps]
-[music stops]

300
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,500
[tense music playing]

301
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,500
[breathing shakily]

302
00:17:53,583 --> 00:17:54,916
Grandma!

303
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:57,291
Grandma! [whimpers]

304
00:17:57,375 --> 00:17:59,250
Talk to me, please. Come on.

305
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:02,541
-Mom, come quick!
-[heart monitor beeping]

306
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,416
[somber music playing]

307
00:18:09,666 --> 00:18:12,791
[Scheyla] <i>Your grandma had a stroke.</i>

308
00:18:12,875 --> 00:18:14,458
We need to be strong, Bruna.

309
00:18:14,541 --> 00:18:15,458
[game chiming]

310
00:18:15,541 --> 00:18:17,041
I'm really gonna need your help.

311
00:18:17,666 --> 00:18:20,291
At the house, at school…

312
00:18:20,375 --> 00:18:23,791
-I'm not gonna… I'm not leaving her here.
-She's in better hands here, okay?

313
00:18:23,875 --> 00:18:25,458
We'll take her home soon.

314
00:18:25,958 --> 00:18:27,416
But it might take a while.

315
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,208
I can't believe you.

316
00:18:29,291 --> 00:18:30,791
You give up without even trying.

317
00:18:30,875 --> 00:18:32,708
Bruna, listen to me.

318
00:18:32,791 --> 00:18:34,500
It's out of our control.

319
00:18:34,583 --> 00:18:36,958
And you should really
call your dad tonight.

320
00:18:37,041 --> 00:18:40,583
Why should I? What does…
does my dad have to do with any of this?

321
00:18:40,666 --> 00:18:44,041
He was your age when his grandma got sick.

322
00:18:44,125 --> 00:18:46,208
And she was the only family he's ever had.

323
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:48,625
You mean because he abandoned ours,
don't you?

324
00:18:48,708 --> 00:18:51,208
Hey, Bruna, what did I tell you?

325
00:18:51,291 --> 00:18:52,875
We have to stick together.

326
00:18:52,958 --> 00:18:54,625
Me, you two, and your father.

327
00:18:54,708 --> 00:18:57,916
I wish just once you would stop
making bullshit excuses for my dad.

328
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,833
I'm not gonna fight with you, Bruna.

329
00:18:59,916 --> 00:19:01,958
Show some respect to your mother.

330
00:19:02,041 --> 00:19:03,666
[cell phone ringing, vibrating]

331
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:08,416
Answer it.

332
00:19:09,291 --> 00:19:11,458
Or are you going to send N.D. from V.A.
to voicemail?

333
00:19:12,666 --> 00:19:15,125
[dramatic music playing]

334
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:19,125
[Scheyla] Bruna, come back here!

335
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:20,791
Enzo, come here.

336
00:19:22,583 --> 00:19:23,833
Bruna! Bruna!

337
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:28,500
Bruna!

338
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:35,791
Hi, my love. How's everything going?

339
00:19:35,875 --> 00:19:37,416
[Scheyla] <i>My mother's in the hospital.</i>

340
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:39,125
She had a stroke.

341
00:19:39,208 --> 00:19:40,333
[ND] <i>A stroke?</i>

342
00:19:41,125 --> 00:19:42,125
Are you okay?

343
00:19:43,583 --> 00:19:44,666
And Bruna is missing.

344
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:46,458
What do you mean
Bruna is missing, Scheyla?

345
00:19:46,541 --> 00:19:47,583
<i>We were at the hospital.</i>

346
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:50,166
We had a fight,
and Bruna bolted out of there.

347
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:53,625
You know her, she runs off, disappears.
She runs, but she always comes back.

348
00:19:53,708 --> 00:19:54,916
How long ago was this?

349
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,416
<i>This morning.</i>
<i>I've been calling, but she won't pick up.</i>

350
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,708
I've called half the city,
nobody's seen her.

351
00:19:59,791 --> 00:20:01,666
Are you saying
my daughter is out on the streets?

352
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:03,166
No one knows where she's at?

353
00:20:03,250 --> 00:20:04,500
[Scheyla] <i>Yes, your daughter!</i>

354
00:20:04,583 --> 00:20:07,333
Because she's just like you.
Stubborn as hell.

355
00:20:08,625 --> 00:20:10,041
Calm down.

356
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,500
Let me think of something.

357
00:20:11,583 --> 00:20:14,708
Well, while you think on it
on the other side of the world,

358
00:20:14,791 --> 00:20:16,208
I'll be looking for her.

359
00:20:17,541 --> 00:20:18,833
[phone line beeping]

360
00:20:18,916 --> 00:20:19,833
[cell phone beeps]

361
00:20:23,166 --> 00:20:25,166
[intriguing music playing]

362
00:20:26,041 --> 00:20:27,208
[Moicano] Let's go to Italy.

363
00:20:27,791 --> 00:20:30,416
You can ride it out there
until we figure out all this.

364
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:33,375
We killed two members
of Petar Ilic's family, bro.

365
00:20:33,958 --> 00:20:36,000
They're gonna hunt us down like rats.

366
00:20:36,083 --> 00:20:37,708
You go alone, man.

367
00:20:37,791 --> 00:20:39,250
I gotta go to Brazil.

368
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:40,666
To Brazil?

369
00:20:41,291 --> 00:20:43,000
You sure that's a good idea, bro?

370
00:20:43,541 --> 00:20:45,750
You make everybody there think
you suddenly died,

371
00:20:45,833 --> 00:20:48,625
so that you can disappear
without so much as a trace,

372
00:20:48,708 --> 00:20:50,166
and now you're going back?

373
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,250
It's been four years, brother.

374
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:54,208
No one remembers me anymore.

375
00:20:54,291 --> 00:20:56,500
-You stay here and take care of business.
-[sighs]

376
00:20:56,583 --> 00:20:58,291
I need to take care of my family.

377
00:20:58,375 --> 00:21:00,041
They're in danger because of me.

378
00:21:00,125 --> 00:21:02,291
I'll call you when I get to Brazil.

379
00:21:05,916 --> 00:21:07,083
We got this, bro.

380
00:21:07,166 --> 00:21:08,083
You have my trust.

381
00:21:10,291 --> 00:21:11,833
I got you, brother.

382
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:16,458
[in Serbian] Let's go to Italy.

383
00:21:16,541 --> 00:21:19,000
-[engine starts]
-[car door closes]

384
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:24,583
[car approaching]

385
00:21:24,666 --> 00:21:25,958
[engine stops]

386
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:29,500
[car door closes]

387
00:21:30,791 --> 00:21:32,041
[breath trembling]

388
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,708
[in English] I don't know what else to do.
She could be anywhere right now.

389
00:21:36,791 --> 00:21:38,541
Take a deep breath, Scheyla.

390
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:40,416
[Scheyla inhales]

391
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,583
A mother has one job.

392
00:21:43,333 --> 00:21:44,333
And I failed.

393
00:21:44,416 --> 00:21:47,833
I ask myself every day,
"Where'd I go wrong?"

394
00:21:47,916 --> 00:21:49,541
[pensive music playing]

395
00:21:49,625 --> 00:21:52,583
Look, my love, I've never been a mother.

396
00:21:53,083 --> 00:21:55,000
But I know what kind of mother you are.

397
00:21:56,458 --> 00:21:58,166
You haven't gone wrong.

398
00:21:58,250 --> 00:21:59,833
She'll come back.

399
00:21:59,916 --> 00:22:01,708
-Okay?
-[Scheyla sniffling]

400
00:22:01,791 --> 00:22:03,625
Have faith. Everything will be okay.

401
00:22:12,125 --> 00:22:13,958
[tense music playing]

402
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:26,916
Documents, please.

403
00:23:01,083 --> 00:23:02,333
Come with me, please.

404
00:23:06,125 --> 00:23:08,500
I have to open your bag, okay?

405
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:31,666
[customs agent 1] All clear?

406
00:23:36,041 --> 00:23:37,458
[customs agent 2] All clear.

407
00:23:41,083 --> 00:23:42,791
Welcome to Brazil, Mr. Lopes.

408
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:48,958
[music fades]

409
00:23:49,041 --> 00:23:51,750
SÃO VICENTE HOSPITAL

410
00:23:51,833 --> 00:23:53,291
[heart monitor beeping]

411
00:23:53,375 --> 00:23:54,666
[breath trembling] Mom.

412
00:23:54,750 --> 00:23:56,041
[pensive music playing]

413
00:23:56,125 --> 00:23:57,333
I…

414
00:23:58,041 --> 00:23:59,916
I try to be a good mother.

415
00:24:01,083 --> 00:24:03,000
I've been remembering…

416
00:24:05,375 --> 00:24:06,583
growing up,

417
00:24:07,625 --> 00:24:10,291
how much worry and trouble
I must've caused.

418
00:24:11,166 --> 00:24:13,000
[sniffles]

419
00:24:14,916 --> 00:24:16,750
I'm so sorry, Mom.

420
00:24:20,666 --> 00:24:21,750
[sniffles]

421
00:24:23,208 --> 00:24:24,750
[breath trembling, sniffles]

422
00:24:26,458 --> 00:24:27,708
[door opens]

423
00:24:37,083 --> 00:24:40,083
No one saw your sister at school today?
You're sure about that, Enzo?

424
00:24:40,166 --> 00:24:42,458
I told you, Mom, no one's seen her.

425
00:24:44,250 --> 00:24:45,291
Dad?

426
00:24:46,125 --> 00:24:47,875
[ND] Hey buddy!

427
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,500
Oh my God! I missed you so much.

428
00:24:52,583 --> 00:24:54,125
-Enzo…
-[ND] When did you get so big?

429
00:24:54,208 --> 00:24:57,083
The present you made your dad at school,
go get it.

430
00:25:00,583 --> 00:25:02,750
What's happening? What are you doing here?

431
00:25:02,833 --> 00:25:04,208
Where's our daughter, Scheyla?

432
00:25:04,291 --> 00:25:05,333
I have it under control.

433
00:25:05,416 --> 00:25:07,041
She should be home by now.

434
00:25:07,125 --> 00:25:08,958
What do you think I've been doing?

435
00:25:10,250 --> 00:25:11,500
You're here to supervise?

436
00:25:11,583 --> 00:25:13,333
[ND] Supervise? Really?

437
00:25:13,416 --> 00:25:16,166
I can't just be concerned
about my family's safety now?

438
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:17,625
[Scheyla] Concerned?

439
00:25:18,583 --> 00:25:20,833
You've been on the other side of the world
this whole time,

440
00:25:20,916 --> 00:25:23,500
but now you're concerned
about your family's safety?

441
00:25:23,583 --> 00:25:25,875
[tense music playing]

442
00:25:25,958 --> 00:25:27,500
[ND] Where were you?

443
00:25:31,083 --> 00:25:34,250
-You tell me right now where you've been.
-Calm down, Luiz Fernando.

444
00:25:36,875 --> 00:25:38,041
I was at a friend's place.

445
00:25:38,125 --> 00:25:39,541
What friend?

446
00:25:39,625 --> 00:25:40,833
A boy.

447
00:25:40,916 --> 00:25:43,833
I slept over by accident,
and I missed school.

448
00:25:43,916 --> 00:25:45,500
[Scheyla] By accident. [scoffs]

449
00:25:47,166 --> 00:25:48,833
Haven't heard of cell phones?

450
00:25:48,916 --> 00:25:52,208
I called you, Bruna. You didn't answer.
Your mother called you. You didn't answer.

451
00:25:55,166 --> 00:25:56,708
It died.

452
00:25:56,791 --> 00:25:58,041
[ND] Your phone was dead?

453
00:25:59,125 --> 00:26:02,083
Okay, you are never stepping foot
out of this house again

454
00:26:02,166 --> 00:26:04,291
without telling your mom first.
Do you understand?

455
00:26:08,166 --> 00:26:10,291
You came all the way here because of this?

456
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:17,041
I was worried.

457
00:26:17,125 --> 00:26:18,500
[footsteps approaching]

458
00:26:21,750 --> 00:26:23,500
[Enzo] This is for you, Dad.

459
00:26:23,583 --> 00:26:24,666
[music fades]

460
00:26:26,166 --> 00:26:27,166
Oh, wow!

461
00:26:29,375 --> 00:26:30,625
It's beautiful.

462
00:26:31,916 --> 00:26:32,916
[kiss]

463
00:26:40,708 --> 00:26:42,333
-You made this at school?
-[Enzo] Uh-huh.

464
00:26:42,416 --> 00:26:45,958
Miss Martins gave each of us
a piece of paper

465
00:26:46,041 --> 00:26:48,916
and told us to draw
a self-portrait of our family.

466
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:51,125
That's awesome, buddy.

467
00:26:51,208 --> 00:26:52,916
I missed you.

468
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,583
[Enzo] I missed you too.

469
00:27:04,791 --> 00:27:06,375
You can sleep here.

470
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:08,125
[pensive music playing]

471
00:27:12,250 --> 00:27:13,083
Hm.

472
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:20,333
You could have given us a heads-up.

473
00:27:21,708 --> 00:27:23,375
To come to my own house?

474
00:27:24,708 --> 00:27:27,291
Is there something going on
that I don't know about?

475
00:27:28,208 --> 00:27:30,416
Is this not still my house?

476
00:27:31,666 --> 00:27:33,333
I'll make sure not to bother you.

477
00:27:33,916 --> 00:27:35,166
[cell phone vibrating]

478
00:27:37,083 --> 00:27:38,166
[cell phone beeps]

479
00:27:39,541 --> 00:27:41,333
[tense music playing]

480
00:27:42,416 --> 00:27:45,666
If you don't want to bother us,
then while you're here, don't leave.

481
00:27:48,375 --> 00:27:51,666
[pensive music playing]

482
00:27:51,750 --> 00:27:54,625
[Joel over phone] <i>Yo, ND,</i>
<i>I'm here with the guys.</i>

483
00:27:54,708 --> 00:27:57,416
<i>Why don't you come by so we can talk</i>
<i>about this shit with the Serbians.</i>

484
00:28:02,291 --> 00:28:04,958
[suspenseful music playing]

485
00:28:13,583 --> 00:28:16,250
-ND.
-[ND] Hey, brother.

486
00:28:17,583 --> 00:28:19,333
[man 1] The rat raised the stakes
too high.

487
00:28:19,416 --> 00:28:22,000
-Thought he had an ace up his sleeve.
-[men laughing]

488
00:28:22,083 --> 00:28:24,041
[man 2] When the deal went south
and things turned,

489
00:28:24,125 --> 00:28:25,708
we sent him straight to hell.

490
00:28:25,791 --> 00:28:26,958
[all laughing]

491
00:28:27,041 --> 00:28:30,083
[man 3] That's the game. Your play, sir.
If you fuck this up, it's over.

492
00:28:30,166 --> 00:28:31,416
[man 2] I'll raise.

493
00:28:31,500 --> 00:28:33,250
Hey boys. ND.

494
00:28:33,333 --> 00:28:35,333
-Yo, ND.
-ND.

495
00:28:35,416 --> 00:28:36,583
[ND] What's up, my brothers?

496
00:28:36,666 --> 00:28:39,833
-[man 3] You want in on the next hand?
-No, no, man. I'm jet-lagged.

497
00:28:39,916 --> 00:28:40,916
Oh, hey, ND,

498
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,916
if you were in Italy, then you'd be
in the same time zone as Serbia, right?

499
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,541
You're funny, brother.

500
00:28:45,625 --> 00:28:48,833
Moicano's over there.
Plan's still going down. Our guy's on it.

501
00:28:48,916 --> 00:28:50,041
So, ND.

502
00:28:50,125 --> 00:28:52,291
It's just that right after you left,

503
00:28:52,375 --> 00:28:54,541
we tried to track him,
but his phone went dark, bro.

504
00:28:54,625 --> 00:28:56,708
And then we had someone send us this.

505
00:28:57,250 --> 00:29:00,416
[dramatic music playing]

506
00:29:00,500 --> 00:29:03,041
The SUV didn't make it to Italy.

507
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:08,416
This doesn't mean anything, man.
This is just another burnt car.

508
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:11,000
Moicano's alive.
He's just up to his bullshit, man.

509
00:29:12,291 --> 00:29:15,083
I was the one that got him
into the business, in Paraná.

510
00:29:15,166 --> 00:29:17,875
If he were up to his bullshit tricks,
I think I'd know, bro.

511
00:29:17,958 --> 00:29:19,208
But my gut says he's not.

512
00:29:20,958 --> 00:29:23,791
You know what? ND is a pretty lucky guy.

513
00:29:23,875 --> 00:29:27,166
He was supposed to go on that car,
but instead he's here with his brothers.

514
00:29:27,250 --> 00:29:28,583
Alive and well. Right, ND?

515
00:29:28,666 --> 00:29:29,666
[man 1] Damn right.

516
00:29:29,750 --> 00:29:31,000
I don't get you, man.

517
00:29:31,083 --> 00:29:32,375
[tense music playing]

518
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:35,458
[Joel] Let's relax.

519
00:29:35,541 --> 00:29:36,458
Hey, Betoneira.

520
00:29:36,541 --> 00:29:39,083
How many years of jail you think
you and I got combined? Thousand?

521
00:29:39,166 --> 00:29:41,375
-Something like that.
-[Joel laughs] Maybe more.

522
00:29:41,458 --> 00:29:43,458
We're old men, on the run.

523
00:29:44,125 --> 00:29:46,541
Let's relax
and not make assumptions, right?

524
00:29:46,625 --> 00:29:47,458
Right, Joel.

525
00:29:47,541 --> 00:29:49,208
[man 2] On a serious note, brothers.

526
00:29:49,291 --> 00:29:53,375
Some of this organization's funds
appear to have gone missing.

527
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,541
We're all aware of that, right?

528
00:29:55,625 --> 00:29:57,750
[tense music continues]

529
00:29:57,833 --> 00:29:59,375
We'll have to take this upstairs.

530
00:29:59,458 --> 00:30:00,541
That's right, brother.

531
00:30:02,291 --> 00:30:05,166
Well, Nando's finally back in town.

532
00:30:05,250 --> 00:30:06,750
He's with his family.

533
00:30:06,833 --> 00:30:09,500
His wife, his kids, his brothers…

534
00:30:09,583 --> 00:30:10,583
And now, Nando…

535
00:30:10,666 --> 00:30:13,750
This is the best made in the world,
Japanese whiskey.

536
00:30:13,833 --> 00:30:16,416
Those guys know how to make
the whiskey I like.

537
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:18,916
It's a worldwide sensation, man. Drink up.

538
00:30:22,875 --> 00:30:24,916
-<i>Arigato!</i>
-[all] <i>Arigato!</i>

539
00:30:29,208 --> 00:30:31,666
-[Betoneira] Look, Platina.
-[Platina] The luck of a cheat, huh?

540
00:30:31,750 --> 00:30:34,333
I'm just lucky, my brother!
Good clean luck!

541
00:30:38,416 --> 00:30:40,208
RECENT
MOICANO - MISSED CALL

542
00:30:40,291 --> 00:30:41,958
[door opens]

543
00:30:46,291 --> 00:30:48,541
-[ND] Good morning.
-Morning.

544
00:30:49,666 --> 00:30:52,750
I was crunching some numbers before bed.

545
00:30:53,375 --> 00:30:55,125
Counting the time I was in prison,

546
00:30:55,208 --> 00:30:57,166
after you were arrested I mean,

547
00:30:57,250 --> 00:30:59,666
we've spent more time apart than together.

548
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:01,583
Can you believe that?

549
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:04,750
Yeah, but we're raising
two children together, Scheyla.

550
00:31:04,833 --> 00:31:05,666
No.

551
00:31:07,166 --> 00:31:09,541
Raising children means being around.
Both of us.

552
00:31:10,791 --> 00:31:13,416
You'll have to wake the kids. I'm leaving.

553
00:31:13,500 --> 00:31:15,250
I'm going to the hospital to see my mom.

554
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:17,833
[keypad clicking]

555
00:31:17,916 --> 00:31:19,500
[knocking on door]

556
00:31:19,583 --> 00:31:20,750
[ND] Sweetheart!

557
00:31:21,458 --> 00:31:22,416
[sighs]

558
00:31:22,916 --> 00:31:23,958
[ND] Bruna!

559
00:31:24,041 --> 00:31:24,875
Enter.

560
00:31:26,708 --> 00:31:27,833
What's up?

561
00:31:28,916 --> 00:31:29,750
Want some breakfast?

562
00:31:29,833 --> 00:31:31,666
You choose it, I'll make it.

563
00:31:32,416 --> 00:31:34,375
[sighs] What do we have to eat?

564
00:31:44,041 --> 00:31:45,083
[sighs]

565
00:32:04,416 --> 00:32:06,958
-[ND] Your brother still hasn't come down.
-[keypad clicking]

566
00:32:07,041 --> 00:32:09,083
You have to wake him up.
He's a heavy sleeper.

567
00:32:10,166 --> 00:32:11,583
Sweetheart, we need to talk.

568
00:32:15,375 --> 00:32:16,541
Am I pissing you off already?

569
00:32:17,916 --> 00:32:18,958
Bruna.

570
00:32:20,208 --> 00:32:22,041
Do you have any idea
what your mom went through

571
00:32:22,125 --> 00:32:23,416
when you ran away?

572
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:24,583
[keypad clicking]

573
00:32:24,666 --> 00:32:26,041
Are you paying attention?

574
00:32:29,250 --> 00:32:30,083
Yup.

575
00:32:30,166 --> 00:32:31,500
So put down your phone already.

576
00:32:33,083 --> 00:32:34,083
[cell phone clicks]

577
00:32:34,583 --> 00:32:36,583
You spend your whole day on that thing.

578
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:40,916
And who's this boy
that you spent the night with?

579
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:43,791
I asked your mom. She doesn't know.

580
00:32:44,833 --> 00:32:46,958
Why have we never heard of him before?

581
00:32:47,041 --> 00:32:48,500
Grandma's heard of him.

582
00:32:49,125 --> 00:32:51,166
Yeah, but your grandma isn't here.

583
00:32:53,833 --> 00:32:55,416
How old is this boy?

584
00:32:56,916 --> 00:32:58,041
Who's his family?

585
00:32:59,125 --> 00:33:01,458
If you don't know my friends
or their parents,

586
00:33:01,541 --> 00:33:03,625
that's not my problem. It's yours.

587
00:33:03,708 --> 00:33:04,833
[ND exhales]

588
00:33:04,916 --> 00:33:07,041
When I call you,
you never answer the phone.

589
00:33:07,708 --> 00:33:09,458
It's been two years since I've seen you.

590
00:33:09,541 --> 00:33:10,958
Because you didn't want to.

591
00:33:11,583 --> 00:33:14,791
If you could've come back this whole time,
then why did you wait this long?

592
00:33:14,875 --> 00:33:16,250
Watch your tone, girl.

593
00:33:16,333 --> 00:33:18,416
All of a sudden you think
you run this house again?

594
00:33:18,500 --> 00:33:21,250
[invigorating music playing]

595
00:33:23,875 --> 00:33:25,125
I'm gonna eat in my room.

596
00:33:25,208 --> 00:33:26,625
Bruna, come back here.

597
00:33:27,166 --> 00:33:28,291
Bruna!

598
00:33:28,375 --> 00:33:30,333
[sizzling]

599
00:33:32,375 --> 00:33:33,375
Shit.

600
00:33:52,375 --> 00:33:53,500
[cell phone chimes]

601
00:33:59,333 --> 00:34:01,000
[Joel] <i>Here's the deal, ND.</i>

602
00:34:01,083 --> 00:34:03,291
<i>We're looking into this Moicano guy.</i>

603
00:34:03,375 --> 00:34:05,916
<i>Don't worry, I'll keep you updated.</i>

604
00:34:07,208 --> 00:34:10,333
[man singing worship song]

605
00:34:36,333 --> 00:34:37,416
[suspenseful music playing]

606
00:34:38,708 --> 00:34:40,041
I can't believe it. Dude!

607
00:34:40,125 --> 00:34:42,750
-[laughing] Is it really you?
-[ND laughing]

608
00:34:43,833 --> 00:34:46,875
-[man] Dude, how you been?
-I've been good. And you?

609
00:34:46,958 --> 00:34:49,916
I'm good. Happy to see you.

610
00:34:51,250 --> 00:34:52,166
[boy chuckling]

611
00:34:52,250 --> 00:34:53,958
[man] Look! Check it out. [laughs]

612
00:34:54,041 --> 00:34:56,291
Your boy's all grown up now.
Congratulations.

613
00:34:56,375 --> 00:34:57,208
Yeah, man.

614
00:34:57,291 --> 00:34:59,833
His mom used to be his favorite,
but now it's me.

615
00:34:59,916 --> 00:35:01,458
Maybe it's just this age.

616
00:35:01,541 --> 00:35:03,416
Yeah, my boy was the same way.

617
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:06,666
Now I'm the father of a teenager
and it's a whole 'nother story.

618
00:35:06,750 --> 00:35:10,000
The second you think you've got it right,
you screw something else up, man.

619
00:35:10,083 --> 00:35:12,625
I can't imagine Chiquinho at that age.

620
00:35:12,708 --> 00:35:14,833
But if my guy's like me,
he'll be chillin'.

621
00:35:14,916 --> 00:35:16,458
You? Chillin'?

622
00:35:16,541 --> 00:35:18,458
-[man laughs]
-[laughing] You're crazy!

623
00:35:18,541 --> 00:35:22,166
Man, Chiquinho might be hyper,
but no one compares to you.

624
00:35:22,250 --> 00:35:24,416
-You remember back in school?
-I remember.

625
00:35:24,500 --> 00:35:27,541
When you and Rita got together.
Man, even I got in trouble.

626
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:29,875
You guys were a nightmare, man. [laughing]

627
00:35:31,375 --> 00:35:33,083
Have you talked to Rita at all lately?

628
00:35:35,083 --> 00:35:36,208
Not yet.

629
00:35:37,666 --> 00:35:39,041
You know what Rita's like, right?

630
00:35:39,125 --> 00:35:41,333
She likes to take her time, no small talk.

631
00:35:41,416 --> 00:35:43,458
But I'll get in touch with her.

632
00:35:44,291 --> 00:35:45,416
That's good.

633
00:35:46,333 --> 00:35:49,291
-So you're back for real this time?
-Nah, man.

634
00:35:49,375 --> 00:35:51,500
Just sorting out some issues at home.

635
00:35:52,208 --> 00:35:54,125
And one of them's called Bruna.
Heard of it?

636
00:35:54,208 --> 00:35:55,333
I have.

637
00:35:56,500 --> 00:35:57,333
You know, man…

638
00:35:57,416 --> 00:35:59,666
Guess who's getting ready
to perform on this stage?

639
00:35:59,750 --> 00:36:00,583
Chiquinho?

640
00:36:01,166 --> 00:36:02,916
The one and only. Bruna.

641
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,041
Seriously, man?

642
00:36:05,125 --> 00:36:06,958
I asked her to perform at a service.

643
00:36:09,291 --> 00:36:12,583
I've only seen her sing once.
I didn't even know that she…

644
00:36:13,291 --> 00:36:14,708
That she liked it that much.

645
00:36:14,791 --> 00:36:16,791
-Well, she does.
-That's cool.

646
00:36:16,875 --> 00:36:18,750
We all have our ways
of expressing ourselves.

647
00:36:18,833 --> 00:36:22,041
Once you understand hers,
I bet she'll listen to you.

648
00:36:22,125 --> 00:36:25,375
[Bruna singing worship song]

649
00:37:00,958 --> 00:37:01,791
[chuckles]

650
00:37:02,375 --> 00:37:03,458
[tense music playing]

651
00:37:03,541 --> 00:37:05,916
[man over phone] <i>First of,</i>
<i>much love to you all, brothers.</i>

652
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,833
<i>I miss the days</i>
<i>when crime meant something.</i>

653
00:37:07,916 --> 00:37:10,833
<i>You know, respect, loyalty,</i>
<i>a code you really lived by.</i>

654
00:37:10,916 --> 00:37:12,833
<i>May God always be on our side.</i>

655
00:37:12,916 --> 00:37:15,708
<i>So I hear there's been some problems</i>
<i>over there. Let's hear it, brothers.</i>

656
00:37:15,791 --> 00:37:18,208
I'll start
by filling you in on everything.

657
00:37:18,291 --> 00:37:21,083
We're here today
because of some missing money

658
00:37:21,166 --> 00:37:23,750
that resulted
in the death of two Serbians,

659
00:37:23,833 --> 00:37:26,000
members of Petar Ilic's family.

660
00:37:26,083 --> 00:37:28,625
And also because of the disappearance

661
00:37:28,708 --> 00:37:31,208
of our brother who's been in Europe. Yeah?

662
00:37:31,291 --> 00:37:33,083
Right, Joel.

663
00:37:33,166 --> 00:37:34,833
That's right, my brothers.

664
00:37:34,916 --> 00:37:38,000
Our comrade Moicano
is presumed to be dead.

665
00:37:38,083 --> 00:37:40,583
We still haven't heard from him yet, true.

666
00:37:41,250 --> 00:37:43,458
But if your godson shows up, Buda,

667
00:37:43,541 --> 00:37:46,666
tell him that we want him to come in
for a debrief, please, okay?

668
00:37:46,750 --> 00:37:49,291
I'm not sure how he'll make it,
if he's dead.

669
00:37:49,375 --> 00:37:50,875
[ND] You think so, bro?

670
00:37:50,958 --> 00:37:53,083
When me and Moicano were in Europe,
he was solid.

671
00:37:54,375 --> 00:37:56,916
We would've taken a bullet for each other.

672
00:37:57,833 --> 00:37:59,958
But when I went
to look up his record, man,

673
00:38:01,333 --> 00:38:02,625
I dug up a ghost.

674
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:08,208
This is a picture of the rat
before plastic surgery.

675
00:38:08,291 --> 00:38:12,708
Paulo Lopes,
who everyone here knows as Moicano,

676
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:13,666
doesn't exist.

677
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:17,458
But who does exist?
Gumercindo Queiroz. "Govinda."

678
00:38:17,541 --> 00:38:19,833
Who was a part of the crew in Roraima.

679
00:38:20,541 --> 00:38:22,666
[man over phone] <i>You lost me, ND.</i>

680
00:38:22,750 --> 00:38:24,583
<i>Explain more clearly, man.</i>

681
00:38:26,125 --> 00:38:27,333
[door opens]

682
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:34,625
Please, take a seat.

683
00:38:37,875 --> 00:38:39,583
Tell them what you told us.

684
00:38:40,125 --> 00:38:41,541
[woman] My name is Rosana.

685
00:38:41,625 --> 00:38:44,708
The man you saw in the photo
is Gumercindo.

686
00:38:45,208 --> 00:38:46,666
My husband.

687
00:38:47,291 --> 00:38:49,791
But he suddenly went missing
a few years ago.

688
00:38:49,875 --> 00:38:53,250
I thought he was dead
or in jail or something, but…

689
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:54,708
But a couple of years passed by,

690
00:38:54,791 --> 00:38:58,083
and my cousin found out
he was living under another name.

691
00:38:58,166 --> 00:38:59,208
Me and my daughter,

692
00:38:59,875 --> 00:39:01,416
we went after him.

693
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:06,166
When he found out
the two of us were looking for him,

694
00:39:06,250 --> 00:39:07,708
he went to Europe.

695
00:39:07,791 --> 00:39:09,000
That's all I know.

696
00:39:09,083 --> 00:39:11,416
I just want to move on with my life.

697
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:14,125
I have no idea
what he's been doing all these years.

698
00:39:14,208 --> 00:39:16,250
My daughter and I
had nothing to do with this.

699
00:39:16,333 --> 00:39:17,541
Please, please don't blame me.

700
00:39:17,625 --> 00:39:20,250
You're just giving us some information.

701
00:39:20,333 --> 00:39:24,583
Rest assured that nothing bad
is going to happen to you or your family.

702
00:39:24,666 --> 00:39:26,125
You can go. Appreciate it.

703
00:39:26,208 --> 00:39:27,041
Walk her out.

704
00:39:27,125 --> 00:39:28,500
No.

705
00:39:30,041 --> 00:39:31,750
I'll give it to him myself.

706
00:39:32,916 --> 00:39:33,750
Goodbye.

707
00:39:38,375 --> 00:39:41,208
Govinda was already a dead man in Roraima.

708
00:39:41,291 --> 00:39:43,083
He'd stolen from one of our brothers.

709
00:39:43,166 --> 00:39:44,750
That's what happened.

710
00:39:44,833 --> 00:39:46,541
[man over phone] <i>I remember.</i>

711
00:39:46,625 --> 00:39:49,208
<i>When we went after that rat,</i>
<i>he disappeared.</i>

712
00:39:49,708 --> 00:39:51,375
[Buda] No, no. You have the wrong guy.

713
00:39:51,458 --> 00:39:53,166
Moicano was baptized in Paraná with me.

714
00:39:53,250 --> 00:39:57,000
Brother, Govinda faked his death
in Roraima, then turned around

715
00:39:57,083 --> 00:40:00,750
and decided he'd be rebaptized
as Moicano in Paraná, man.

716
00:40:00,833 --> 00:40:02,041
Don't you get it?

717
00:40:02,125 --> 00:40:04,750
Are you trying to say
this organization is a failure?

718
00:40:04,833 --> 00:40:06,500
That we're all idiots?

719
00:40:06,583 --> 00:40:09,041
And that we can't keep track
of our own members?

720
00:40:09,125 --> 00:40:11,541
Why are you putting words
in my mouth, brother?

721
00:40:11,625 --> 00:40:12,666
Is that what I said?

722
00:40:13,250 --> 00:40:15,583
Everyone here
has their own responsibilities.

723
00:40:15,666 --> 00:40:17,375
Everyone here has their own jobs to do.

724
00:40:17,458 --> 00:40:20,125
We're supposed to background check
everyone in this organization?

725
00:40:21,416 --> 00:40:23,125
And this guy had a fake ID, brother.

726
00:40:23,208 --> 00:40:26,750
He took advantage of a flawed system
and became someone else, right?

727
00:40:26,833 --> 00:40:30,041
[man over phone] <i>Got any proof of this?</i>
<i>Where're you getting these ideas from?</i>

728
00:40:30,916 --> 00:40:32,375
[sighs]

729
00:40:34,291 --> 00:40:36,500
That's him, in Portugal.

730
00:40:36,583 --> 00:40:39,250
Days after his car went up in flames.

731
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:40,916
Look at the scar on his hand, it's him.

732
00:40:44,291 --> 00:40:47,583
Moicano stole our money
and blamed the Serbians.

733
00:40:48,833 --> 00:40:50,791
And then he made a run for it.

734
00:40:50,875 --> 00:40:54,958
Buda, explain it to your brothers.
How could you baptize a maniac like that?

735
00:40:55,541 --> 00:40:57,875
Man, he seemed like a good dude.

736
00:40:57,958 --> 00:41:00,375
He was responsible, never made a mistake.

737
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:03,083
[man over phone] <i>That rat was thrown out</i>
<i>because he betrayed us.</i>

738
00:41:03,166 --> 00:41:06,041
<i>He disappears</i>
<i>and comes back to fuck us over again?</i>

739
00:41:06,125 --> 00:41:08,041
<i>That's why</i>
<i>these streets are a fucking mess.</i>

740
00:41:08,125 --> 00:41:10,291
<i>Everybody stealing from each other,</i>
<i>killing each other.</i>

741
00:41:10,375 --> 00:41:13,375
<i>And none of you have</i>
<i>your own brothers' backs anymore.</i>

742
00:41:14,916 --> 00:41:17,583
That rat may have gotten away
the first time.

743
00:41:17,666 --> 00:41:20,125
Now he's getting
motherfucking exterminated.

744
00:41:20,208 --> 00:41:21,250
Straight up.

745
00:41:21,333 --> 00:41:22,916
[man over phone] <i>That's right.</i>

746
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:26,458
<i>God may be the judge,</i>
<i>but we give the verdict.</i>

747
00:41:26,541 --> 00:41:28,625
<i>Those traitors can go straight to hell.</i>

748
00:41:29,458 --> 00:41:31,041
<i>Find him, brothers.</i>

749
00:41:31,125 --> 00:41:33,583
<i>Buda, you're his godfather.</i>

750
00:41:33,666 --> 00:41:35,500
<i>This is your responsibility.</i>

751
00:41:35,583 --> 00:41:37,000
<i>Finish the job.</i>

752
00:41:37,875 --> 00:41:40,625
With all due respect, brothers.

753
00:41:40,708 --> 00:41:43,083
I would like to make it clear
I'll be taking care of this one.

754
00:41:44,166 --> 00:41:47,958
[man] <i>If you're willing to put your neck</i>
<i>on the line, then the job's yours, man.</i>

755
00:41:48,041 --> 00:41:50,125
<i>Whatever you have planned</i>
<i>for that fucking snake,</i>

756
00:41:50,208 --> 00:41:51,750
<i>don't let it take too long.</i>

757
00:41:51,833 --> 00:41:53,041
<i>Let this be an example.</i>

758
00:41:53,125 --> 00:41:55,625
<i>And make it very painful. You got that?</i>

759
00:41:57,708 --> 00:42:00,041
Moicano's turning
into our bargaining chip with the Serbs.

760
00:42:00,625 --> 00:42:01,458
Good!

761
00:42:01,541 --> 00:42:05,375
[man over phone] <i>The order's officially</i>
<i>been given, ND. We good?</i>

762
00:42:07,250 --> 00:42:08,708
[music fades]

763
00:42:09,708 --> 00:42:12,166
-[school bell ringing]
-[indistinct chatter]

764
00:42:14,958 --> 00:42:16,791
There's no way this is gonna work.

765
00:42:16,875 --> 00:42:18,375
Stay calm.

766
00:42:23,125 --> 00:42:25,000
-Yo, let's move! Let's move.
-Come on!

767
00:42:26,875 --> 00:42:27,833
[both chuckling]

768
00:42:27,916 --> 00:42:29,083
[Bruna] Careful!

769
00:42:31,583 --> 00:42:34,125
If I get failed for ditching,
my mom'll kill me.

770
00:42:34,208 --> 00:42:36,750
Especially with my grandma
in the hospital.

771
00:42:36,833 --> 00:42:37,666
[boy] How is she?

772
00:42:38,791 --> 00:42:40,000
She's better.

773
00:42:40,583 --> 00:42:44,250
They finally took her off the ventilator,
but she's still in the ICU.

774
00:42:45,791 --> 00:42:47,333
I know it might be a while.

775
00:42:48,541 --> 00:42:50,000
But she'll be fine.

776
00:42:53,958 --> 00:42:57,375
[Bruna] I planted those flowers with her
after we moved here.

777
00:42:58,291 --> 00:42:59,666
Where'd you move here from?

778
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:02,958
Everywhere you could possibly think of.

779
00:43:03,041 --> 00:43:06,916
I think I've moved more times
than probably anyone else in history.

780
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:07,833
But why?

781
00:43:12,583 --> 00:43:13,750
Come on!

782
00:43:14,250 --> 00:43:16,291
You know so much about me already.

783
00:43:17,166 --> 00:43:19,083
You've even been to my place.

784
00:43:19,583 --> 00:43:22,041
I told you my dad has another family.

785
00:43:22,125 --> 00:43:23,916
But you won't tell me anything.

786
00:43:30,791 --> 00:43:31,750
There you go.

787
00:43:32,750 --> 00:43:34,583
-Now you know.
-[chuckles]

788
00:43:36,583 --> 00:43:37,791
Tell me more.

789
00:44:00,125 --> 00:44:02,250
You and the kids are gonna have to move.

790
00:44:02,916 --> 00:44:03,791
Are you serious?

791
00:44:04,416 --> 00:44:05,708
Nando, I love this house.

792
00:44:05,791 --> 00:44:07,875
It's close to the kids' school
and my salon.

793
00:44:07,958 --> 00:44:09,375
It's a safe neighborhood.

794
00:44:09,458 --> 00:44:11,375
Scheyla, I have to get out of Serbia.

795
00:44:12,333 --> 00:44:14,500
And I want this family somewhere safer.

796
00:44:14,583 --> 00:44:18,541
You're kidding me. Always a sacrifice.
How about you compromise for once?

797
00:44:18,625 --> 00:44:20,125
Why don't you just go alone again?

798
00:44:21,125 --> 00:44:23,166
This is none of your business, Bruna.

799
00:44:23,250 --> 00:44:25,208
-Please go to your room, Bruna.
-Or what?

800
00:44:25,291 --> 00:44:26,416
You're gonna slap me again?

801
00:44:27,583 --> 00:44:30,333
Why can't you be more understanding,
more like your little brother?

802
00:44:32,041 --> 00:44:33,208
Cause maybe, unlike me,

803
00:44:33,791 --> 00:44:36,208
my brother hasn't figured out
you'll be leaving again soon,

804
00:44:36,291 --> 00:44:38,291
and you won't be back
for who knows how long.

805
00:44:38,958 --> 00:44:40,458
[intercom ringing]

806
00:44:50,583 --> 00:44:51,791
<i>Hey, did someone order pizza?</i>

807
00:44:53,166 --> 00:44:55,375
[woman] We thought
you'd like the surprise.

808
00:44:56,291 --> 00:44:58,916
-[Scheyla] Yes, somebody did order pizza.
-[man 1] What's up?

809
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:01,458
You look so handsome, Chiquinho.

810
00:45:01,541 --> 00:45:04,458
-[man 2] How's it going, Scheyla?
-[Scheyla] Aww. How are you?

811
00:45:04,541 --> 00:45:06,458
-[man 1] Boo-yah.
-[woman] Hi, my love.

812
00:45:07,083 --> 00:45:08,541
[Scheyla] Can you take that, honey?

813
00:45:08,625 --> 00:45:11,750
Guys, make yourselves at home.
Our house is your house.

814
00:45:13,833 --> 00:45:15,541
-Damn, bro.
-[ND] Shit!

815
00:45:15,625 --> 00:45:17,083
[man 2] Good to see you. How are you?

816
00:45:17,166 --> 00:45:18,833
-[ND] How are you, man?
-Too long, dude.

817
00:45:18,916 --> 00:45:21,000
-How you been?
-[ND] Doing good.

818
00:45:21,083 --> 00:45:23,250
-You cleaned up a little, huh, bud?
-You noticed, huh?

819
00:45:23,333 --> 00:45:26,291
Could almost pass for a businessman
with this fit.

820
00:45:26,375 --> 00:45:27,250
You know it.

821
00:45:27,333 --> 00:45:29,666
-And the bikes?
-No, it's in the past now.

822
00:45:29,750 --> 00:45:32,208
-Now I just Uber everywhere, bro.
-End of an era.

823
00:45:32,291 --> 00:45:34,208
I'll go help in the kitchen.
It's good to see you.

824
00:45:37,125 --> 00:45:38,125
[ND] Rita.

825
00:45:57,750 --> 00:46:00,291
-Hey.
-[chuckling] Hey.

826
00:46:02,958 --> 00:46:06,291
-The three amigos together again, huh?
-[both] Yeah.

827
00:46:06,375 --> 00:46:09,708
-I've missed you guys.
-So have we.

828
00:46:09,791 --> 00:46:12,500
-Thanks, that's plenty.
-[Enzo] Press this one to make him jump…

829
00:46:12,583 --> 00:46:16,000
Buddy, take Chiquinho
to play video games in your room, okay?

830
00:46:16,083 --> 00:46:18,000
Let's go play upstairs, Chiquinho.

831
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,750
I was gonna tell you I was back.

832
00:46:28,833 --> 00:46:31,791
I just needed some time
to try to get my head straight.

833
00:46:31,875 --> 00:46:32,708
[Rita] I figured.

834
00:46:33,916 --> 00:46:35,250
I'll get over it.

835
00:46:35,791 --> 00:46:36,791
[sighs]

836
00:46:36,875 --> 00:46:39,416
I missed my family like crazy.

837
00:46:40,250 --> 00:46:41,833
Well, actually I missed you all.

838
00:46:43,791 --> 00:46:46,708
Yeah, I know you and I might be going
through a rough patch right now,

839
00:46:46,791 --> 00:46:50,125
but I must admit, I really did miss you.

840
00:46:50,208 --> 00:46:51,958
[both laughing]

841
00:46:52,041 --> 00:46:54,041
-You seem really good.
-Hmm.

842
00:46:54,125 --> 00:46:56,750
[ND] It's nice to see you like this.
You deserve it.

843
00:46:57,458 --> 00:46:58,750
Thank you, brother.

844
00:46:59,666 --> 00:47:00,750
I feel happy.

845
00:47:00,833 --> 00:47:02,750
-We have to make a toast, my friend.
-Okay.

846
00:47:02,833 --> 00:47:04,583
[upbeat music playing]

847
00:47:06,583 --> 00:47:10,208
Since the whole family's here tonight,
let's raise a glass to Laura.

848
00:47:10,291 --> 00:47:12,500
[Scheyla] Thank God
she's getting better. [sighs]

849
00:47:12,583 --> 00:47:14,416
-To Laura.
-[all] To Laura.

850
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:18,791
I thought you would love the pizza idea.
Remember the last time we did this?

851
00:47:18,875 --> 00:47:19,791
At Rita's house, right?

852
00:47:20,375 --> 00:47:23,250
How could I forget, right?
Chiquinho threw up all over me.

853
00:47:23,333 --> 00:47:24,333
-Disgusting.
-Oh, no!

854
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:26,041
That was a crazy night.

855
00:47:26,125 --> 00:47:29,750
Let's move on to something nicer.
Shall we talk about our star's big debut?

856
00:47:29,833 --> 00:47:31,541
-[Scheyla] How do you feel?
-Just nervous.

857
00:47:31,625 --> 00:47:33,833
Everyone has it
in their planners, right, guys?

858
00:47:34,500 --> 00:47:36,500
Well, all but one.

859
00:47:38,375 --> 00:47:40,750
[chuckling awkwardly]

860
00:47:40,833 --> 00:47:44,416
You know, if it weren't for your dad,
I wouldn't be a singer, don't you?

861
00:47:44,500 --> 00:47:47,458
-[Bruna] What do you mean?
-The first song I ever wrote was stolen.

862
00:47:47,541 --> 00:47:50,166
And if it weren't for this guy here,
there'd be no MC Doni.

863
00:47:50,250 --> 00:47:52,500
You used to be, like, MC Don…

864
00:47:52,583 --> 00:47:55,958
-Dondoka.
-Dondoka. That's right.

865
00:47:56,666 --> 00:47:57,875
[Bruna] Who's Dondoka?

866
00:47:57,958 --> 00:48:00,250
At the time, she was the biggest MC, yeah?

867
00:48:00,333 --> 00:48:02,250
-[Scheyla] Yeah, she was.
-[ND] She was huge.

868
00:48:02,333 --> 00:48:03,750
You hear that, honey?

869
00:48:03,833 --> 00:48:06,541
Your old man was once an MC's manager.
Pretty cool.

870
00:48:06,625 --> 00:48:08,708
[Rita] An MC's manager…

871
00:48:08,791 --> 00:48:10,708
How about the wrestling matches
at those shows?

872
00:48:11,583 --> 00:48:14,083
[Scheyla] Oh my God.

873
00:48:15,125 --> 00:48:17,000
I remember it like it was yesterday,

874
00:48:17,083 --> 00:48:19,333
that beating you took from Jussara,
remember?

875
00:48:19,416 --> 00:48:21,583
How could I let myself forget
something like that?

876
00:48:21,666 --> 00:48:22,583
Your coworker, Jussara?

877
00:48:22,666 --> 00:48:25,625
That's the one. My God, she was crazy.

878
00:48:27,041 --> 00:48:29,416
Imagine, me against her.
Who do you think got the worst of it?

879
00:48:29,500 --> 00:48:31,250
-You, right, Auntie?
-[Rita] Ding, ding, ding.

880
00:48:31,333 --> 00:48:33,250
But no one could beat that woman though.

881
00:48:33,333 --> 00:48:36,208
Wait, didn't she try
to kick your ass too, Formiga?

882
00:48:36,291 --> 00:48:39,291
We were at a party,
and someone ended up breaking her cooler.

883
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:41,000
For some reason she thought I did it.

884
00:48:41,083 --> 00:48:42,916
It wasn't enough
that she'd beaten up your aunt,

885
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:44,458
she wanted to beat up your uncle now.

886
00:48:44,541 --> 00:48:45,583
Think I stood up to her?

887
00:48:45,666 --> 00:48:48,375
She was nuts back then,
but she's better now, huh?

888
00:48:48,458 --> 00:48:50,250
Well, kinda.

889
00:48:50,333 --> 00:48:51,875
[Rita] Nah, I doubt it.

890
00:48:51,958 --> 00:48:53,458
[all laughing]

891
00:48:54,291 --> 00:48:56,750
[tense music playing]

892
00:49:00,250 --> 00:49:02,208
[Joel] I told the Serbians
we wanted to meet

893
00:49:02,291 --> 00:49:04,250
to straighten out this whole fuckin' mess.

894
00:49:04,333 --> 00:49:05,625
[ND] That's perfect.

895
00:49:05,708 --> 00:49:08,250
Let's hand over the rat and settle this.

896
00:49:35,250 --> 00:49:36,083
[Joel] Ilic.

897
00:49:36,833 --> 00:49:40,083
We're here as a sign of respect for you
and our longstanding partnership.

898
00:49:42,541 --> 00:49:43,791
And to prove it.

899
00:49:46,458 --> 00:49:47,666
Moicano.

900
00:49:48,750 --> 00:49:51,750
He's the one who stole the money
that was missing from the deal.

901
00:49:51,833 --> 00:49:53,791
[Joel] We're very sorry for your loss.

902
00:49:53,875 --> 00:49:56,333
But that bastard's grave
is already dug for you.

903
00:49:56,416 --> 00:49:59,291
And next month's shipment
is free of charge, okay?

904
00:50:00,625 --> 00:50:02,916
I was born in Yugoslavia.

905
00:50:03,625 --> 00:50:05,250
I fight in the Bosnian War.

906
00:50:05,833 --> 00:50:08,166
I see many comrades die in battle.

907
00:50:08,250 --> 00:50:10,125
I was tortured.

908
00:50:10,833 --> 00:50:13,333
All of this, I can forget.

909
00:50:13,416 --> 00:50:17,000
But the thing
I can never be able to forget,

910
00:50:17,083 --> 00:50:19,125
your men have killed my family.

911
00:50:19,958 --> 00:50:24,041
This I will carry with me forever.
Someone must pay for this.

912
00:50:26,208 --> 00:50:28,666
But business is business.

913
00:50:29,291 --> 00:50:31,666
And the money must keep moving.

914
00:50:45,500 --> 00:50:47,083
[tense music builds]

915
00:50:47,166 --> 00:50:48,750
-[gunshots]
-Shit, Joel. What the fuck?

916
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:52,666
-Watch out. Hide!
-[Joel] Hurry, ND. Come on, let's go!

917
00:50:54,125 --> 00:50:55,375
[grunting]

918
00:50:56,750 --> 00:50:57,750
[groans]

919
00:50:57,833 --> 00:50:59,875
[ND] We're fucked, man.
There's more. There's more!

920
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:03,875
[tires screeching]

921
00:51:09,666 --> 00:51:10,708
[grunts]

922
00:51:11,208 --> 00:51:12,375
[exploding]

923
00:51:13,125 --> 00:51:14,666
-[gunshots]
-[Joel] Now, N.D.

924
00:51:15,375 --> 00:51:16,916
Let's get outta here!

925
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:18,541
[gunshots]

926
00:51:21,375 --> 00:51:22,666
[grunting]

927
00:51:28,208 --> 00:51:29,833
[groaning]

928
00:51:39,250 --> 00:51:41,083
[ND] So it was you, Buda?

929
00:51:42,083 --> 00:51:43,750
I knew you were a snake.

930
00:51:44,250 --> 00:51:46,875
-You know you're gonna die, bro.
-[Buda groaning]

931
00:51:46,958 --> 00:51:49,541
I'm gonna kill you,
and then I'm gonna kill your partner.

932
00:51:49,625 --> 00:51:52,125
You're both going straight to hell, rat.

933
00:51:54,125 --> 00:51:56,791
-[keypad clicking]
-[Buda groaning]

934
00:51:56,875 --> 00:51:59,500
[cell phone ringing]

935
00:51:59,583 --> 00:52:02,041
[ambient music playing]

936
00:52:02,125 --> 00:52:03,125
Hey, Buda.

937
00:52:03,208 --> 00:52:04,916
You get the job done already?

938
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:06,750
[ND over phone] <i>Hi, Govinda.</i>

939
00:52:07,333 --> 00:52:09,375
<i>Did you really believe</i>
<i>you would screw everybody over</i>

940
00:52:09,458 --> 00:52:10,958
<i>and get away with it?</i>

941
00:52:12,333 --> 00:52:14,125
<i>You dug your own grave.</i>

942
00:52:14,625 --> 00:52:16,541
[dramatic music playing]

943
00:52:26,875 --> 00:52:29,625
[hip-hop music playing over speakers]

944
00:52:37,083 --> 00:52:38,416
Stop.

945
00:52:40,750 --> 00:52:42,333
What's wrong?

946
00:52:42,416 --> 00:52:43,458
Nothing.

947
00:52:43,541 --> 00:52:45,291
-Everything okay?
-Mm-hmm.

948
00:52:49,291 --> 00:52:50,708
It's just that

949
00:52:52,375 --> 00:52:54,458
I've never had a guy over to the house.

950
00:52:55,458 --> 00:52:57,083
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

951
00:52:57,166 --> 00:52:59,666
-I'm special I guess, huh? [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

952
00:53:00,250 --> 00:53:01,458
[music stops]

953
00:53:02,875 --> 00:53:03,708
Your grandma?

954
00:53:05,625 --> 00:53:07,791
I'll go visit her later tonight.

955
00:53:12,125 --> 00:53:12,958
Your dad?

956
00:53:14,625 --> 00:53:17,541
Wow, you look just like him here. Uh…

957
00:53:20,166 --> 00:53:21,333
Sorry.

958
00:53:22,250 --> 00:53:24,416
You get like this
every time we talk about him.

959
00:53:24,500 --> 00:53:25,958
I guess I just wanted to know why.

960
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:32,750
Fuck, that's my bad.
Sorry, I shouldn't have…

961
00:53:34,291 --> 00:53:36,916
Hey, if you wanna talk to me,
I wanna listen.

962
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:38,125
I understand.

963
00:53:38,916 --> 00:53:40,791
-[exhales]
-Trust me.

964
00:53:40,875 --> 00:53:42,041
Murilo…

965
00:53:43,416 --> 00:53:44,291
Yeah?

966
00:53:44,791 --> 00:53:46,208
You have to promise you won't tell.

967
00:53:46,750 --> 00:53:48,166
Tell… Tell what?

968
00:53:48,250 --> 00:53:50,416
Just promise this stays
between you and me, okay?

969
00:53:51,750 --> 00:53:53,750
-But why do I need to promise…
-Please, Murilo.

970
00:53:53,833 --> 00:53:55,291
Okay, okay. I promise.

971
00:53:55,916 --> 00:53:57,666
[pensive music playing]

972
00:53:59,166 --> 00:54:00,916
My dad is N.D. from V.A.

973
00:54:01,833 --> 00:54:02,666
Who's that?

974
00:54:04,583 --> 00:54:05,916
He was a drug dealer.

975
00:54:07,625 --> 00:54:08,791
What?

976
00:54:09,666 --> 00:54:11,250
Like, do you mean…

977
00:54:11,333 --> 00:54:12,666
Like mob cartel shit? [chuckles]

978
00:54:14,500 --> 00:54:15,458
[cell phone clicks]

979
00:54:15,541 --> 00:54:16,708
[keypad clicks]

980
00:54:16,791 --> 00:54:20,708
[man] <i>One of the leaders of São Paulo's</i>
<i>most powerful criminal organization,</i>

981
00:54:20,791 --> 00:54:23,541
<i>Luiz Fernando Silva,</i>
<i>also known as N.D. from V.A.,</i>

982
00:54:23,625 --> 00:54:26,166
<i>was arrested last Friday</i>
<i>in downtown São Paulo…</i>

983
00:54:26,250 --> 00:54:27,500
Holy fucking shit.

984
00:54:29,291 --> 00:54:31,583
I remember that. Fuck.
That… That's your old man?

985
00:54:32,166 --> 00:54:34,166
Does that mean your dad's killed people?

986
00:54:34,250 --> 00:54:36,250
-No, he's not a…
-Does your dad keep his guns here?

987
00:54:36,333 --> 00:54:38,541
-No, of course he doesn't. I'm… I mean…
-This is insane!

988
00:54:38,625 --> 00:54:41,958
-Like, oh my God. I'm, like, what…
-Look, Murilo, forget about it, okay?

989
00:54:42,041 --> 00:54:43,541
-Just forget I said anything.
-Uh…

990
00:54:43,625 --> 00:54:46,875
I think you should probably go,
and we can talk more about it later.

991
00:54:46,958 --> 00:54:49,625
I'll text you. Please, just go.

992
00:54:49,708 --> 00:54:53,541
-Okay. Sorry for being…
-Murilo, I said we'll talk about it later.

993
00:54:56,416 --> 00:54:58,125
It's just a lot to take in.

994
00:55:02,333 --> 00:55:03,666
Listen…

995
00:55:05,750 --> 00:55:08,583
I'm not like my father. Okay?

996
00:55:09,541 --> 00:55:10,583
I know.

997
00:55:12,375 --> 00:55:13,541
Come here.

998
00:55:15,166 --> 00:55:17,458
Relax, okay? I'm not gonna tell anyone.

999
00:55:18,208 --> 00:55:20,125
-Come here.
-Look…

1000
00:55:21,791 --> 00:55:23,375
You should go.

1001
00:55:23,458 --> 00:55:26,083
We can talk about it another time, okay?

1002
00:55:27,375 --> 00:55:30,291
Okay.

1003
00:55:31,041 --> 00:55:31,916
See you tomorrow?

1004
00:55:40,083 --> 00:55:41,458
[door closes]

1005
00:55:48,041 --> 00:55:49,708
[Bruna] <i>You were right, Grandma.</i>

1006
00:55:50,791 --> 00:55:51,916
[sighs]

1007
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:54,416
I should've given it more time,
like you told me to.

1008
00:55:57,375 --> 00:56:00,708
We all make mistakes, my dear.
They're a part of life.

1009
00:56:00,791 --> 00:56:03,500
What's important
is that you learned from it.

1010
00:56:04,291 --> 00:56:08,958
It shows that you are way more mature
than me or your mom were at your age.

1011
00:56:09,041 --> 00:56:10,541
[Grandma chuckles]

1012
00:56:10,625 --> 00:56:11,916
[door opens]

1013
00:56:15,875 --> 00:56:17,333
Be right back.

1014
00:56:22,208 --> 00:56:24,583
-I love you.
-I love you more.

1015
00:56:28,333 --> 00:56:29,958
[Grandma chuckles]

1016
00:56:38,583 --> 00:56:39,666
Laura…

1017
00:56:49,708 --> 00:56:52,250
I know I'm probably the last guy
you wanna see right now.

1018
00:56:52,333 --> 00:56:54,208
[breathing shakily]

1019
00:56:54,916 --> 00:56:57,125
[ND] But I came here to apologize.

1020
00:56:58,791 --> 00:57:00,500
I wanna thank you…

1021
00:57:02,708 --> 00:57:04,458
for being so wonderful
to your grandchildren.

1022
00:57:04,541 --> 00:57:06,083
You mean the world to them.

1023
00:57:08,375 --> 00:57:10,708
Thank you for taking care of my family.

1024
00:57:29,041 --> 00:57:32,375
[Grandma] When I first met you,
you were just a boy.

1025
00:57:33,958 --> 00:57:35,625
[chuckles]

1026
00:57:35,708 --> 00:57:38,416
I may not have given birth to you…

1027
00:57:40,458 --> 00:57:43,458
but God knows
how much I suffered over you.

1028
00:57:46,250 --> 00:57:50,250
He knows how I worried.
And He knows all the sleep I lost.

1029
00:57:50,333 --> 00:57:51,833
You took years off my life.

1030
00:57:51,916 --> 00:57:54,333
[chuckles, sighs]

1031
00:57:55,875 --> 00:57:58,041
Oh, my son…

1032
00:57:59,416 --> 00:58:01,375
You need to know…

1033
00:58:03,166 --> 00:58:05,625
You are powerful, son.

1034
00:58:05,708 --> 00:58:08,666
Your strength has always been
your greatest virtue.

1035
00:58:09,916 --> 00:58:13,791
I see a lot of that strength
in my grandchildren.

1036
00:58:14,666 --> 00:58:17,333
When are you finally going to slow down

1037
00:58:17,416 --> 00:58:22,208
and realize what really matters the most
in your life, my dear?

1038
00:58:22,791 --> 00:58:23,958
What will it take?

1039
00:58:24,041 --> 00:58:26,708
Your children turning their backs on you?

1040
00:58:29,291 --> 00:58:31,083
Enough.

1041
00:58:31,166 --> 00:58:34,291
Just look what you've done to this family.

1042
00:58:37,958 --> 00:58:41,166
My time is coming to an end very soon.

1043
00:58:42,250 --> 00:58:45,125
And I will no longer be here
to keep you in line.

1044
00:58:46,041 --> 00:58:47,750
And to tell you…

1045
00:58:49,916 --> 00:58:51,666
Forget the past.

1046
00:58:51,750 --> 00:58:54,541
The future is in your hands.
You must know that.

1047
00:58:56,208 --> 00:58:58,208
It's time to make a change.

1048
00:58:58,291 --> 00:59:00,791
[breathing heavily]

1049
00:59:03,000 --> 00:59:04,750
Prove us all wrong, son.

1050
00:59:05,916 --> 00:59:07,125
Hmm?

1051
00:59:08,125 --> 00:59:10,125
Do it for your children.

1052
00:59:24,750 --> 00:59:26,250
[ND] God bless you.

1053
00:59:26,750 --> 00:59:28,500
[Grandma] God bless you too.

1054
00:59:39,375 --> 00:59:42,625
Do you think Grandma is giving up?

1055
00:59:48,916 --> 00:59:49,875
[ND groans]

1056
00:59:52,291 --> 00:59:54,458
You've lost a lot of people, huh?

1057
00:59:55,166 --> 00:59:56,333
Yeah.

1058
00:59:58,291 --> 01:00:00,041
But it never seems to get easier.

1059
01:00:02,458 --> 01:00:03,291
Why?

1060
01:00:04,916 --> 01:00:07,791
Because I've hurt too many people
in this life, Bruna.

1061
01:00:09,875 --> 01:00:12,583
But I've always tried to do right
by the people I love the most.

1062
01:00:13,875 --> 01:00:15,166
Really?

1063
01:00:16,208 --> 01:00:18,166
Honey, I never knew my father.

1064
01:00:18,250 --> 01:00:19,833
I didn't have a mother.

1065
01:00:20,625 --> 01:00:23,625
No one asked me
what I wanted to do when I grew up.

1066
01:00:24,875 --> 01:00:26,916
That was my childhood.

1067
01:00:30,708 --> 01:00:33,833
This job was the only option I had
at the time

1068
01:00:35,500 --> 01:00:37,875
to give you,
your mom, your little brother…

1069
01:00:39,833 --> 01:00:42,083
to give you a better life than I ever had.

1070
01:00:46,500 --> 01:00:48,291
You're right. We've had

1071
01:00:49,500 --> 01:00:51,083
a much better life.

1072
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:56,125
But honestly, in my opinion,

1073
01:00:56,833 --> 01:00:58,583
love means
being present for your children.

1074
01:01:07,833 --> 01:01:09,666
[upbeat music playing]

1075
01:01:12,166 --> 01:01:13,500
And also…

1076
01:01:15,833 --> 01:01:17,750
you look ridiculous in that black hat.

1077
01:01:21,125 --> 01:01:22,291
You think?

1078
01:01:23,041 --> 01:01:24,375
[Bruna] I know.

1079
01:01:25,375 --> 01:01:29,625
-Then how about I put on the glasses?
-[laughing] No. Don't do that.

1080
01:01:36,750 --> 01:01:38,458
-[knocking on door]
-[ND] Scheyla?

1081
01:01:42,583 --> 01:01:43,916
[music fades]

1082
01:01:45,166 --> 01:01:46,750
The kids are in bed.

1083
01:01:46,833 --> 01:01:48,333
[dreamy music playing]

1084
01:01:49,208 --> 01:01:52,041
I was wondering if you needed anything.

1085
01:01:52,125 --> 01:01:54,416
I was on my way to bed too.

1086
01:02:19,958 --> 01:02:21,750
I've missed this.

1087
01:02:23,041 --> 01:02:24,708
Sleeping in the bed?

1088
01:02:25,750 --> 01:02:27,250
I meant you.

1089
01:02:33,291 --> 01:02:34,708
[Scheyla sighs]

1090
01:03:13,750 --> 01:03:15,083
Nando,

1091
01:03:15,833 --> 01:03:17,458
if you leave me,

1092
01:03:18,333 --> 01:03:19,666
promise me

1093
01:03:20,166 --> 01:03:22,208
you won't ever come back.

1094
01:03:30,875 --> 01:03:32,000
[music ends]

1095
01:03:32,083 --> 01:03:33,916
CAETANO SOARES SCHOOL

1096
01:03:39,291 --> 01:03:42,041
BRUNA: NEED TO TALK TO U
MURILO: WHAT'S UP?

1097
01:03:42,125 --> 01:03:44,875
BRUNA: MEET ME IN THE HALLWAY

1098
01:03:48,250 --> 01:03:49,541
[cell phone vibrates]

1099
01:03:53,125 --> 01:03:55,125
[intriguing music playing]

1100
01:04:02,500 --> 01:04:05,083
[school bell ringing]

1101
01:04:05,166 --> 01:04:08,291
[indistinct chatter]

1102
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:13,458
[inaudible]

1103
01:04:16,500 --> 01:04:19,333
[cell phones chiming]

1104
01:04:20,125 --> 01:04:21,000
[girl scoffs]

1105
01:04:23,125 --> 01:04:24,916
[keypad clicking]

1106
01:04:31,708 --> 01:04:33,833
WANNABE GANGSTA

1107
01:04:33,916 --> 01:04:35,666
SHE'LL SCAM U WITH THAT DIRTY MONEY

1108
01:04:35,750 --> 01:04:37,291
BRO YOU'RE CRAZY FOR THIS

1109
01:04:37,375 --> 01:04:39,375
[cell phones chiming]

1110
01:04:39,458 --> 01:04:41,250
[students murmuring]

1111
01:04:44,708 --> 01:04:45,958
[cell phones chiming]

1112
01:04:46,041 --> 01:04:48,000
[students laughing]

1113
01:05:02,583 --> 01:05:05,041
-What did you say? Who did you tell?
-Calm down. Calm down.

1114
01:05:05,125 --> 01:05:06,416
-My bad, it's just…
-[laughs]

1115
01:05:06,500 --> 01:05:08,166
So now everyone at school
knows about this?

1116
01:05:08,250 --> 01:05:09,375
I know.

1117
01:05:10,125 --> 01:05:11,000
I might've told Kiko.

1118
01:05:11,083 --> 01:05:12,708
You swore to me you wouldn't tell anybody.

1119
01:05:12,791 --> 01:05:15,625
-You broke your word after you promised.
-I know, Bruna. And I'm sorry.

1120
01:05:15,708 --> 01:05:18,625
No! Sorry doesn't begin to fix
the mess you've created.

1121
01:05:18,708 --> 01:05:20,333
-Wait, Bruna. Bruna.
-[cell phones chiming]

1122
01:05:21,166 --> 01:05:22,375
[exhales]

1123
01:05:23,541 --> 01:05:24,416
Fuck.

1124
01:05:25,291 --> 01:05:26,250
What are you looking at?

1125
01:05:26,333 --> 01:05:28,250
[upbeat music playing]

1126
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:32,041
[whirring]

1127
01:05:35,875 --> 01:05:38,708
-Hey, how are you, my love?
-Hi Jussara, how are you?

1128
01:05:38,791 --> 01:05:40,333
Good, my love. Good.

1129
01:05:40,416 --> 01:05:42,791
Hey. Come here. Come here.

1130
01:05:42,875 --> 01:05:46,500
-What's all this? Glowing, are we now?
-It's nothing, Jussara.

1131
01:05:46,583 --> 01:05:49,875
Tell me, girl. Did you go out last night?
I bet you got your freak on, huh?

1132
01:05:49,958 --> 01:05:51,375
-Stop it!
-Scheyla, hey!

1133
01:05:51,458 --> 01:05:54,750
I just, you know…
For once, I'm not stressed out.

1134
01:05:54,833 --> 01:05:56,708
I know when you're lying.
I'd never judge you.

1135
01:05:56,791 --> 01:05:58,458
-I know that.
-Scheyla, for the love of God.

1136
01:05:58,541 --> 01:06:00,666
-Everything's fine.
-With all you've been going through…

1137
01:06:00,750 --> 01:06:01,708
You deserve it, my love.

1138
01:06:01,791 --> 01:06:04,791
With your mom, with Bruna.
There's a lot on your plate, Schey.

1139
01:06:04,875 --> 01:06:06,291
Things are getting better, okay?

1140
01:06:06,375 --> 01:06:08,458
You're beautiful.
You've got a rockin' bod,

1141
01:06:08,541 --> 01:06:10,333
you're a great mom,
successful businesswoman.

1142
01:06:10,416 --> 01:06:13,416
Babe, if I were your age,
I'd be hooking up with everyone.

1143
01:06:13,500 --> 01:06:15,125
Anytime, anywhere. Everyone and his uncle.

1144
01:06:15,208 --> 01:06:17,041
-You know why I can relax a little?
-Hm?

1145
01:06:17,125 --> 01:06:19,458
-Because I have a partner like you.
-[cell phone ringing]

1146
01:06:19,541 --> 01:06:20,375
Sorry, gimme a sec.

1147
01:06:20,458 --> 01:06:23,125
Okay. Wow, would ya look at that.
She's addicted to that thing.

1148
01:06:23,208 --> 01:06:24,500
God, I love her.

1149
01:06:25,916 --> 01:06:27,041
Hello?

1150
01:06:27,125 --> 01:06:30,833
Well, Scheyla. As you know,
we've been having some issues with Bruna.

1151
01:06:30,916 --> 01:06:31,958
Right?

1152
01:06:32,541 --> 01:06:35,625
But this time,
she's actually assaulted another student.

1153
01:06:36,750 --> 01:06:39,291
Unfortunately, we've run out of patience.

1154
01:06:41,291 --> 01:06:43,416
Well, I'm very sorry to tell you this.

1155
01:06:44,416 --> 01:06:46,375
But the school board has met.

1156
01:06:46,458 --> 01:06:48,458
And we think
it's in everyone’s best interest

1157
01:06:48,541 --> 01:06:50,125
that your daughter leaves this school.

1158
01:06:50,791 --> 01:06:52,000
I don't get it.

1159
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:54,250
Scheyla, letting Bruna stay here

1160
01:06:54,333 --> 01:06:56,166
with everything
your family's going through

1161
01:06:56,250 --> 01:06:57,291
may be detrimental.

1162
01:06:57,375 --> 01:06:58,625
This includes Enzo, of course.

1163
01:06:58,708 --> 01:07:00,875
-Just tell me.
-We wouldn't want him being bullied.

1164
01:07:00,958 --> 01:07:03,000
Tell me what's actually going on.

1165
01:07:03,083 --> 01:07:04,375
You can be honest here.

1166
01:07:04,458 --> 01:07:05,875
I can handle it.

1167
01:07:07,083 --> 01:07:08,208
All right.

1168
01:07:11,458 --> 01:07:16,000
<i>The man you made out</i>
<i>to be a villain, N.D. from V.A., is dead.</i>

1169
01:07:17,166 --> 01:07:19,500
-Now I get it.
-Scheyla, it would be too difficult--

1170
01:07:19,583 --> 01:07:21,250
I'll be taking my kids out of this school.

1171
01:07:21,333 --> 01:07:22,291
But not because of this.

1172
01:07:22,375 --> 01:07:24,791
Because I want to!
Because you aren't doing anything…

1173
01:07:24,875 --> 01:07:26,125
-Calm down.
-…to protect them.

1174
01:07:26,208 --> 01:07:28,833
You're letting these morons
judge my children.

1175
01:07:28,916 --> 01:07:31,166
Scheyla, the parents
will keep on pressuring us.

1176
01:07:31,250 --> 01:07:32,583
It'll become unavoidable.

1177
01:07:32,666 --> 01:07:35,833
Because they're all perfect.
And I'm the only one who's ever messed up.

1178
01:07:36,458 --> 01:07:37,583
And just so we're clear,

1179
01:07:37,666 --> 01:07:42,166
none of those assholes on your board
know me or my life.

1180
01:07:42,250 --> 01:07:44,000
[dramatic music playing]

1181
01:07:44,875 --> 01:07:47,291
[Enzo] Mom, why do we have to leave early?

1182
01:07:47,375 --> 01:07:48,458
We'll talk about it at home.

1183
01:07:50,083 --> 01:07:51,958
Brunita, get in the car.

1184
01:07:52,666 --> 01:07:53,541
Okay.

1185
01:07:55,166 --> 01:07:58,000
You two, what are you lookin' at?

1186
01:07:58,083 --> 01:07:59,416
Fuck off.

1187
01:08:08,625 --> 01:08:09,708
So what happened?

1188
01:08:13,916 --> 01:08:15,958
[tires screeching]

1189
01:08:19,708 --> 01:08:21,291
[tense music playing]

1190
01:08:23,041 --> 01:08:25,041
[engine revving]

1191
01:08:35,833 --> 01:08:37,291
[engine revving]

1192
01:08:37,375 --> 01:08:38,916
[tires screeching]

1193
01:08:50,166 --> 01:08:51,375
[breathing shakily]

1194
01:08:51,458 --> 01:08:52,625
[music fades]

1195
01:08:52,708 --> 01:08:54,375
[reporter] <i>A series of explosions</i>
<i>in Europe</i>

1196
01:08:54,458 --> 01:08:56,125
<i>has left two dead and one wounded</i>

1197
01:08:56,208 --> 01:08:58,666
<i>in what authorities are calling</i>
<i>a suspected criminal dispute.</i>

1198
01:08:58,750 --> 01:09:01,083
<i>The target,</i>
<i>businessman Gumercindo Queiroz,</i>

1199
01:09:01,166 --> 01:09:02,416
<i>known as "Moicano,"</i>

1200
01:09:02,500 --> 01:09:05,250
<i>has surrendered to authorities</i>
<i>at the Brazilian Embassy,</i>

1201
01:09:05,333 --> 01:09:06,875
<i>where he awaits transfer to Brazil</i>

1202
01:09:06,958 --> 01:09:09,166
<i>-…to assist federal authorities…</i>
-Go to your room.

1203
01:09:13,250 --> 01:09:15,041
Nando, I think I was followed.

1204
01:09:15,125 --> 01:09:17,416
-What do you mean, Scheyla?
-Someone followed me.

1205
01:09:17,500 --> 01:09:20,541
-What'd they look like?
-I don't fucking know. They followed us.

1206
01:09:21,500 --> 01:09:22,916
I… I told someone about you.

1207
01:09:23,000 --> 01:09:24,666
[tense music playing]

1208
01:09:24,750 --> 01:09:26,375
But I made them swear they wouldn't tell.

1209
01:09:27,291 --> 01:09:28,791
What is going on here?

1210
01:09:31,541 --> 01:09:34,208
[Scheyla] Everyone at her school
knows who you are.

1211
01:09:34,291 --> 01:09:36,125
And a car just followed us, okay?

1212
01:09:40,541 --> 01:09:42,333
What the fuck have you done, Bruna?

1213
01:09:43,291 --> 01:09:45,000
I already apologized to Mom.

1214
01:09:45,083 --> 01:09:47,750
Sorry doesn't take back
the shit you told your friend.

1215
01:09:47,833 --> 01:09:49,833
What did you tell them I do, Bruna?

1216
01:09:50,791 --> 01:09:53,250
-Dad, I didn't wanna say anything.
-Oh, you didn't want to?

1217
01:09:53,333 --> 01:09:56,875
Now our whole family is in danger
because of you, Bruna.

1218
01:09:56,958 --> 01:09:59,458
You better go upstairs to your room,
right now, okay?

1219
01:10:00,541 --> 01:10:01,833
Go!

1220
01:10:03,625 --> 01:10:05,125
The fuck was that?

1221
01:10:05,208 --> 01:10:06,750
[door slams]

1222
01:10:07,666 --> 01:10:10,333
Listen, this isn't only her fault.

1223
01:10:10,416 --> 01:10:12,000
It's mine then?

1224
01:10:12,083 --> 01:10:14,625
I just want to protect my family, Scheyla.

1225
01:10:14,708 --> 01:10:17,291
If you want to have a family,
you have to understand

1226
01:10:17,375 --> 01:10:19,791
that you don't get to make the calls
on your own.

1227
01:10:19,875 --> 01:10:20,958
I already warned you.

1228
01:10:21,041 --> 01:10:24,083
If you're gonna be here, then be here.

1229
01:10:24,166 --> 01:10:26,208
Or leave and don't come back.

1230
01:10:35,250 --> 01:10:37,250
[invigorating music playing]

1231
01:10:53,500 --> 01:10:54,958
-[Joel] Hey, brother.
-What's up, ND?

1232
01:10:55,041 --> 01:10:57,041
-[man 1] What's good, bro?
-You good, man?

1233
01:10:57,125 --> 01:11:00,125
Hey, ND. Everything good?

1234
01:11:01,083 --> 01:11:02,708
ND, I've got our brother on the line.

1235
01:11:02,791 --> 01:11:05,500
He wants to have a word with you,
talk about a few things.

1236
01:11:05,583 --> 01:11:08,916
Whenever you're ready, my brother.
We've got him right here for you.

1237
01:11:09,958 --> 01:11:11,291
[man 2 over phone] <i>Yo, ND.</i>

1238
01:11:11,375 --> 01:11:13,166
<i>The good news is,</i>
<i>you killed one rat, brother.</i>

1239
01:11:13,250 --> 01:11:16,083
<i>Bad news is, you let the other one live.</i>

1240
01:11:16,166 --> 01:11:18,333
<i>Now what? What if he talks?</i>

1241
01:11:20,666 --> 01:11:21,916
[man 1] Here's the thing.

1242
01:11:22,000 --> 01:11:25,208
You’re not acting like someone
in your position oughta act, ND.

1243
01:11:25,291 --> 01:11:28,000
All you've done is waste our time,
and you haven't fixed anything.

1244
01:11:29,041 --> 01:11:30,916
[man 3] The order was given, was it not?

1245
01:11:31,000 --> 01:11:33,583
And now you've gone and left us
with all your mess.

1246
01:11:33,666 --> 01:11:36,041
[man 2] <i>He's right, man.</i>
<i>Now we're all in danger.</i>

1247
01:11:36,958 --> 01:11:39,041
<i>What are we gonna do about this? Tell me.</i>

1248
01:11:39,125 --> 01:11:40,583
I'll take care of it, man.

1249
01:11:41,458 --> 01:11:43,000
But the thing is, my brothers,

1250
01:11:43,083 --> 01:11:45,500
that piece of shit is flying in
as we speak

1251
01:11:45,583 --> 01:11:47,333
with his very own police escort.

1252
01:11:47,416 --> 01:11:48,583
So how do you expect to do it?

1253
01:11:48,666 --> 01:11:52,250
If we go down, I can promise you
I'm going down with you.

1254
01:11:52,333 --> 01:11:55,375
Don't worry, I'll smash that rat
with my own two hands, man.

1255
01:11:55,458 --> 01:11:57,166
[man 3] Now you're talking.

1256
01:11:57,250 --> 01:11:59,000
Catch that rat and make him pay.

1257
01:11:59,083 --> 01:12:03,125
Better get moving though,
because that bastard lands in two days.

1258
01:12:03,208 --> 01:12:04,625
You've made your point.

1259
01:12:04,708 --> 01:12:07,833
ND is our brother and my partner.

1260
01:12:07,916 --> 01:12:10,583
And speed is his specialty, my brothers.

1261
01:12:10,666 --> 01:12:13,750
[man 2] <i>That's it, then.</i>
<i>ND'll take care of it.</i>

1262
01:12:15,208 --> 01:12:16,791
<i>Watch yourself, ND.</i>

1263
01:12:16,875 --> 01:12:19,375
<i>All the heat's on you now. You got that?</i>

1264
01:12:20,375 --> 01:12:22,833
Understood, brother.
I've got this. I won't let you down.

1265
01:12:23,625 --> 01:12:26,000
-[man 1] You got this, ND.
-[man 2] Thanks, brother.

1266
01:12:28,375 --> 01:12:30,708
[tense music continues]

1267
01:12:34,375 --> 01:12:35,583
That asshole!

1268
01:12:38,750 --> 01:12:41,208
[cell phone vibrating]

1269
01:12:43,791 --> 01:12:44,750
Hi, Scheyla.

1270
01:12:44,833 --> 01:12:47,750
[Scheyla crying] <i>Luiz Fernando, the…</i>

1271
01:12:47,833 --> 01:12:50,541
<i>My mom, she's not…</i>

1272
01:12:50,625 --> 01:12:52,291
<i>She didn't make it.</i>

1273
01:12:52,375 --> 01:12:54,208
[somber music playing]

1274
01:12:56,541 --> 01:12:58,333
[crying]

1275
01:13:29,000 --> 01:13:31,458
Your grandma loved you so much.

1276
01:13:45,625 --> 01:13:47,250
[Scheyla] Thank you. [crying]

1277
01:13:48,458 --> 01:13:51,041
-[Rita] She's so proud of you.
-[Scheyla] Thank you.

1278
01:13:56,041 --> 01:13:58,208
She is, okay?

1279
01:14:30,916 --> 01:14:32,083
I'm glad you're here.

1280
01:14:34,875 --> 01:14:37,250
What difference
does my sitting in the car do?

1281
01:14:41,458 --> 01:14:43,250
When my wife is in there.

1282
01:14:44,833 --> 01:14:47,291
She just buried her mother,
and I can't be there for her.

1283
01:14:51,166 --> 01:14:53,708
My daughter's drifting
further and further away from me.

1284
01:14:55,208 --> 01:14:57,500
Everyone in my house is constantly

1285
01:14:58,000 --> 01:15:01,291
pointing out just how much harm I cause

1286
01:15:02,125 --> 01:15:03,500
when I'm around them.

1287
01:15:03,583 --> 01:15:05,208
[pensive music playing]

1288
01:15:07,875 --> 01:15:09,500
I don't know anymore.

1289
01:15:12,875 --> 01:15:14,708
I'm so tired, Rita.

1290
01:15:22,791 --> 01:15:24,083
Know what I think?

1291
01:15:26,250 --> 01:15:28,875
I think I know you too well,
Luiz Fernando.

1292
01:15:30,375 --> 01:15:32,291
I got to know N.D. from V.A.

1293
01:15:32,791 --> 01:15:33,875
and Nando,

1294
01:15:34,500 --> 01:15:36,166
whom I love.

1295
01:15:36,250 --> 01:15:38,333
My brother, my best friend.

1296
01:15:40,333 --> 01:15:42,916
But I also got to know
that sweet little kid,

1297
01:15:43,000 --> 01:15:45,916
the boy who quit school
to take care of his sick grandmother.

1298
01:15:46,750 --> 01:15:48,625
Who became a father too soon,

1299
01:15:48,708 --> 01:15:50,916
without even having a father of his own.

1300
01:15:51,000 --> 01:15:54,625
You know what all those versions of you
have in common?

1301
01:15:55,166 --> 01:15:56,000
Do you?

1302
01:15:58,791 --> 01:16:00,750
Unconditional love for your family.

1303
01:16:05,500 --> 01:16:07,750
That's why I believe in you, my brother.

1304
01:16:07,833 --> 01:16:09,541
I'm always on your side.

1305
01:16:13,416 --> 01:16:14,541
Thank you.

1306
01:16:18,916 --> 01:16:19,791
I love you.

1307
01:16:20,375 --> 01:16:22,125
I love you even more.

1308
01:16:28,958 --> 01:16:31,875
[Bruna singing worship song]

1309
01:16:53,666 --> 01:16:56,125
It's really painful
to lose someone you love.

1310
01:17:02,208 --> 01:17:04,250
Grandma used to say that

1311
01:17:05,583 --> 01:17:08,083
when we decide to close
one chapter of a book

1312
01:17:09,833 --> 01:17:11,125
we begin a brand new one.

1313
01:17:22,291 --> 01:17:25,000
This is the only thing
I have left of my grandma.

1314
01:17:28,583 --> 01:17:32,833
She gave it to me
when I said I wanted to be a singer.

1315
01:17:34,250 --> 01:17:35,625
A singer?

1316
01:17:36,416 --> 01:17:37,416
[ND] Yeah.

1317
01:17:38,125 --> 01:17:39,625
A guy can dream, right?

1318
01:17:41,500 --> 01:17:43,791
But life had other plans for me.

1319
01:17:53,958 --> 01:17:55,791
The day that you were born…

1320
01:17:58,166 --> 01:17:59,166
[Bruna sniffles]

1321
01:17:59,833 --> 01:18:02,125
…was the happiest day of my life.

1322
01:18:08,375 --> 01:18:11,583
It was as if I'd finally found
the family I never had, in a way.

1323
01:18:17,458 --> 01:18:19,416
How long will you be sticking around
this time?

1324
01:18:23,000 --> 01:18:24,583
Dad, answer me.

1325
01:18:25,625 --> 01:18:26,708
Stop running away.

1326
01:18:27,833 --> 01:18:29,750
Please, just say something.

1327
01:18:31,458 --> 01:18:33,791
Is it important for you to have me here?

1328
01:18:37,083 --> 01:18:38,166
Very.

1329
01:18:48,750 --> 01:18:51,208
If I haven't told you before…

1330
01:18:54,833 --> 01:18:56,125
I really am sorry.

1331
01:19:12,833 --> 01:19:14,625
[tense music playing]

1332
01:19:18,166 --> 01:19:20,375
[sirens wailing in distance]

1333
01:19:29,166 --> 01:19:30,916
[ND] <i>Lord Jesus…</i>

1334
01:19:35,625 --> 01:19:38,458
<i>I know I'm not worthy of your forgiveness.</i>

1335
01:19:38,541 --> 01:19:41,625
<i>I've lived in the darkness</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

1336
01:19:47,208 --> 01:19:48,541
[door opens]

1337
01:19:49,916 --> 01:19:55,291
[ND] <i>Lord, I ask that you take my family</i>
<i>and my home beneath your wings.</i>

1338
01:19:56,625 --> 01:19:59,291
<i>Watch over those I love</i>

1339
01:19:59,375 --> 01:20:02,166
<i>and protect those who love me.</i>

1340
01:20:11,916 --> 01:20:14,291
<i>I know it's a lot to ask,</i>

1341
01:20:14,375 --> 01:20:17,916
<i>but pray that you forgive me</i>
<i>for what I am about to do.</i>

1342
01:20:24,208 --> 01:20:29,375
<i>I pray for the strength, for the courage</i>
<i>to do what needs to be done.</i>

1343
01:20:33,166 --> 01:20:35,166
[engine whirring]

1344
01:20:35,250 --> 01:20:38,958
[indistinct announcement over PA]

1345
01:20:41,583 --> 01:20:46,083
[ND] <i>May the blood shed today</i>
<i>be the last of its kind.</i>

1346
01:20:46,166 --> 01:20:48,000
[keypad clicking]

1347
01:20:48,083 --> 01:20:49,875
[cell phone chimes, vibrates]

1348
01:20:49,958 --> 01:20:52,291
THE TARGET HAS LANDED

1349
01:20:55,791 --> 01:20:57,208
[intriguing music playing]

1350
01:21:02,833 --> 01:21:06,083
[ND] <i>May those</i>
<i>who were unlucky enough to cross my path</i>

1351
01:21:07,250 --> 01:21:09,625
<i>be worthy of your grace.</i>

1352
01:21:21,083 --> 01:21:22,458
[engine starts]

1353
01:21:23,625 --> 01:21:25,958
[wailing]

1354
01:21:29,625 --> 01:21:33,375
[ND] <i>This hell ends today.</i>

1355
01:21:33,458 --> 01:21:34,833
<i>Amen.</i>

1356
01:21:35,666 --> 01:21:37,750
[engine idling]

1357
01:21:39,125 --> 01:21:41,875
In position, waiting on the Feds.

1358
01:21:43,791 --> 01:21:45,750
[sirens approaching]

1359
01:21:51,458 --> 01:21:52,958
The rat's on the run.

1360
01:22:02,791 --> 01:22:04,166
Escort in position, let's roll.

1361
01:22:14,666 --> 01:22:17,625
[man over radio] <i>Heads-up,</i>
<i>the cops are approaching the roadblock.</i>

1362
01:22:18,250 --> 01:22:19,458
[ND] In sight.

1363
01:22:24,541 --> 01:22:28,125
[cop 1] Route blocked by construction,
traffic is stopped, over.

1364
01:22:31,333 --> 01:22:33,583
[cop 2 over radio] <i>Copy, 15-01.</i>
<i>Stay on high alert.</i>

1365
01:22:43,000 --> 01:22:44,083
[gunshot]

1366
01:22:44,166 --> 01:22:45,541
[man] Come on, ND, get 'em!

1367
01:22:47,583 --> 01:22:49,416
[cop 1] Command, we're under attack!

1368
01:22:59,291 --> 01:23:00,166
Get the fuck out!

1369
01:23:00,791 --> 01:23:02,500
Get the fuck out! Get out!

1370
01:23:03,250 --> 01:23:05,375
[man] Get on the ground! On the ground!

1371
01:23:05,458 --> 01:23:08,500
[Joel] ND, get down here.
Cops are on their way.

1372
01:23:12,208 --> 01:23:14,208
[groaning]

1373
01:23:15,666 --> 01:23:18,125
[cop 2 over radio] <i>Unit two,</i>
<i>backup is on the way.</i>

1374
01:23:18,208 --> 01:23:21,208
<i>Unit two, confirm,</i>
<i>are there any casualties?</i>

1375
01:23:21,291 --> 01:23:23,541
<i>Requesting immediate confirmation.</i>

1376
01:23:24,208 --> 01:23:26,125
[triumphant music playing]

1377
01:23:43,250 --> 01:23:45,666
[ND grunting] Get the fuck out,
you fucking rat.

1378
01:23:45,750 --> 01:23:47,958
You never had a family, huh?
You piece of shit.

1379
01:23:48,041 --> 01:23:50,375
[dramatic music playing]

1380
01:23:50,458 --> 01:23:52,291
[breathing heavily]

1381
01:23:54,125 --> 01:23:56,583
I was just playing the same game
you were, brother.

1382
01:23:56,666 --> 01:23:58,416
Only mine was better.

1383
01:23:58,500 --> 01:24:01,500
You put your family at risk
the whole time, didn't you?

1384
01:24:01,583 --> 01:24:04,583
You think my family was my weakness, man?

1385
01:24:05,916 --> 01:24:07,041
No.

1386
01:24:08,291 --> 01:24:10,666
My family's not my weakness.
They're my strength.

1387
01:24:10,750 --> 01:24:12,791
You know this won't be the last time.

1388
01:24:13,291 --> 01:24:14,791
For me, it will be.

1389
01:24:16,583 --> 01:24:18,000
[bullet casing clinking]

1390
01:24:25,541 --> 01:24:26,750
Ilic.

1391
01:24:27,375 --> 01:24:30,375
[Ilic] Now everything is settled
between us.

1392
01:24:30,958 --> 01:24:33,000
We can go on with business.

1393
01:24:33,083 --> 01:24:35,166
As usual, partner.

1394
01:24:37,291 --> 01:24:41,875
[cop 2 over radio] <i>Command to unit two,</i>
<i>backup dispatched, units are on their way.</i>

1395
01:24:41,958 --> 01:24:45,125
<i>Backup is on its way.</i>
<i>Backup is on its way.</i>

1396
01:24:45,208 --> 01:24:48,041
[sirens approaching]

1397
01:24:48,125 --> 01:24:51,791
[singing worship song]

1398
01:25:01,291 --> 01:25:02,750
Say it out loud if you believe it!

1399
01:25:47,541 --> 01:25:49,333
[congregation applauds, cheers]

1400
01:25:52,583 --> 01:25:56,083
I would now like to invite Bruna
to join me up on stage,

1401
01:25:56,166 --> 01:25:59,500
who will be singing with us in praise
and pay tribute to her grandmother.

1402
01:25:59,583 --> 01:26:01,958
Let's make some noise for her, guys.

1403
01:26:02,041 --> 01:26:04,458
[congregation applauds]

1404
01:26:05,500 --> 01:26:06,375
Ready?

1405
01:26:08,208 --> 01:26:11,208
-[applauds fade]
-[soft music playing]

1406
01:26:11,291 --> 01:26:12,791
[Formiga] She's a star.

1407
01:26:14,416 --> 01:26:17,750
[Bruna singing worship song]

1408
01:26:45,666 --> 01:26:46,833
[inaudible]

1409
01:27:38,500 --> 01:27:40,791
Put your hands in the air, my friends!

1410
01:27:40,875 --> 01:27:42,750
Let us praise Him as one voice. Come on!

1411
01:27:42,833 --> 01:27:43,916
[inaudible]

1412
01:28:21,750 --> 01:28:24,708
-[song ends]
-[congregation applauding, cheering]

1413
01:28:27,000 --> 01:28:28,875
Well done! That's so good.

1414
01:28:30,208 --> 01:28:32,041
We love you, honey.

1415
01:28:37,208 --> 01:28:40,583
-What an incredible show, huh?
-I'm so proud of her.

1416
01:28:40,666 --> 01:28:44,458
-Of course you are. She's a mini Doni.
-You're right.

1417
01:28:44,541 --> 01:28:46,208
So this is officially farewell then?

1418
01:28:46,291 --> 01:28:48,166
[inhales] Yeah.

1419
01:28:48,750 --> 01:28:52,625
It's just that after losing my mom
and what happened with the school,

1420
01:28:52,708 --> 01:28:56,041
I'm just ready
to start over somewhere else.

1421
01:28:56,125 --> 01:28:57,291
What about Nando?

1422
01:28:58,541 --> 01:29:00,375
[intriguing music playing]

1423
01:29:01,625 --> 01:29:04,500
[man 1 over phone] <i>Yo, my brothers.</i>
<i>We're here today to celebrate.</i>

1424
01:29:04,583 --> 01:29:06,166
<i>The rat's finally been exterminated.</i>

1425
01:29:07,166 --> 01:29:09,083
<i>What do you say, ND?</i>

1426
01:29:09,666 --> 01:29:11,208
[ND] It's just sad.

1427
01:29:11,875 --> 01:29:13,541
It's sad that this had to happen,

1428
01:29:13,625 --> 01:29:16,458
that another one of our brothers
betrayed us.

1429
01:29:16,541 --> 01:29:18,375
And paid the price for it.

1430
01:29:19,041 --> 01:29:20,333
But let this serve as a reminder

1431
01:29:20,416 --> 01:29:22,041
that there's no place for greed
amongst us.

1432
01:29:22,125 --> 01:29:24,666
-[Joel] Absolutely.
-That's right, brother.

1433
01:29:25,333 --> 01:29:26,250
[man 1] <i>I agree, ND.</i>

1434
01:29:26,333 --> 01:29:28,666
<i>It's not the first time</i>
<i>we've seen this happen.</i>

1435
01:29:28,750 --> 01:29:30,041
<i>There's only one rule, brother.</i>

1436
01:29:30,125 --> 01:29:31,833
<i>No matter how big you get,</i>

1437
01:29:31,916 --> 01:29:34,750
<i>you break your oath,</i>
<i>we make an example outta you.</i>

1438
01:29:34,833 --> 01:29:36,375
Still, we got a problem.

1439
01:29:36,458 --> 01:29:40,333
Moicano's in the ground,
but he took all our money with him.

1440
01:29:40,833 --> 01:29:42,375
[man 1] <i>That's true, brother.</i>

1441
01:29:42,458 --> 01:29:46,041
<i>The money Moicano stole from us</i>
<i>is what feeds our families, isn't it?</i>

1442
01:29:46,750 --> 01:29:48,708
<i>How we gonna make up for this loss, ND?</i>

1443
01:29:50,416 --> 01:29:53,541
Don't worry, the money will be
in everyone's accounts tomorrow.

1444
01:29:53,625 --> 01:29:55,000
I'll cover the difference.

1445
01:29:55,666 --> 01:29:57,125
[man 1] <i>Thank you, ND.</i>

1446
01:29:57,208 --> 01:29:59,416
<i>You've taken responsibility for this mess.</i>

1447
01:29:59,500 --> 01:30:02,875
<i>It's clear when someone comes along</i>
<i>who's built for this life.</i>

1448
01:30:02,958 --> 01:30:06,041
<i>And it's even more clear when someone</i>
<i>pours his blood, sweat, and tears</i>

1449
01:30:06,125 --> 01:30:07,625
<i>into this organization.</i>

1450
01:30:07,708 --> 01:30:10,291
<i>We've followed your journey here</i>
<i>over the years, ND.</i>

1451
01:30:10,375 --> 01:30:13,666
<i>From the beginning, you built up</i>
<i>this family with your loyalty and respect.</i>

1452
01:30:13,750 --> 01:30:16,333
<i>And it's time for your dedication</i>
<i>to be recognized, right?</i>

1453
01:30:16,416 --> 01:30:19,000
<i>It's time for you</i>
<i>to take on a bigger role.</i>

1454
01:30:19,083 --> 01:30:21,291
<i>We’re talking about real leadership here.</i>

1455
01:30:21,375 --> 01:30:23,791
<i>The coastal cities</i>
<i>are this business's lifeblood.</i>

1456
01:30:23,875 --> 01:30:26,666
<i>We're gonna send you to run things</i>
<i>in Santa Catarina.</i>

1457
01:30:26,750 --> 01:30:28,083
<i>How does that sound?</i>

1458
01:30:28,625 --> 01:30:30,416
This is it, ND.

1459
01:30:30,916 --> 01:30:32,625
You'll be with your family, man.

1460
01:30:33,250 --> 01:30:35,791
You'll run the port of Itajaí.

1461
01:30:35,875 --> 01:30:38,625
You and the family'll live
on the beach, brother.

1462
01:30:38,708 --> 01:30:39,625
[Betoneira] Hell yeah.

1463
01:30:39,708 --> 01:30:43,625
You'll manage our finances. Off the radar.

1464
01:30:43,708 --> 01:30:46,083
Well? Are we agreed?

1465
01:30:46,166 --> 01:30:48,083
[Betoneira] Shake his hand.

1466
01:30:49,791 --> 01:30:52,250
I appreciate
everything you've done for me.

1467
01:30:53,833 --> 01:30:55,750
Because when we get
into this line of work,

1468
01:30:55,833 --> 01:30:58,375
it's to save ourselves
from the world out there, you know?

1469
01:30:59,250 --> 01:31:02,000
I've learned a lot over the years
in this business.

1470
01:31:02,750 --> 01:31:04,916
But it comes with a sacrifice, brothers.

1471
01:31:07,083 --> 01:31:09,416
My family's paid the price for it.

1472
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:14,541
My wife went to prison because of me.

1473
01:31:15,833 --> 01:31:18,208
My kids are growing up without a father.

1474
01:31:20,291 --> 01:31:23,166
And despite all that,
my wife stuck right by my side.

1475
01:31:24,875 --> 01:31:28,250
But I still have two kids at home
who need me around, you know?

1476
01:31:34,625 --> 01:31:36,625
So, brothers, as of today,

1477
01:31:36,708 --> 01:31:38,333
I've decided I'm stepping back.

1478
01:31:38,916 --> 01:31:40,750
-The fuck is this?
-[Betoneira] What?

1479
01:31:41,375 --> 01:31:43,000
I'm officially leaving the game.

1480
01:31:43,083 --> 01:31:44,458
[Betoneira] You're fucking with us.

1481
01:31:44,541 --> 01:31:46,500
You forgotten your oath, ND?

1482
01:31:47,125 --> 01:31:50,166
[man 2] Once you read this, you pledge,
with one hundred percent certainty,

1483
01:31:50,250 --> 01:31:52,541
your loyalty to this brotherhood.

1484
01:31:52,625 --> 01:31:55,791
You know that's not how this works,
you can't just walk away.

1485
01:31:55,875 --> 01:31:59,500
Everything you have, everything you are,
is thanks to this organization.

1486
01:31:59,583 --> 01:32:01,333
Who do you think you are without us, huh?

1487
01:32:01,416 --> 01:32:03,208
[ND] <i>This organization does not permit</i>

1488
01:32:03,291 --> 01:32:08,500
dishonesty, collusion, envy, slander,
betrayal, cowardice, or corruption.

1489
01:32:08,583 --> 01:32:11,375
It is my vow to be instead a servant,

1490
01:32:11,458 --> 01:32:13,916
a voice for change, a warrior,

1491
01:32:14,000 --> 01:32:17,083
and a guardian,
in pursuit of the common good.

1492
01:32:17,166 --> 01:32:20,333
Because we are all for one
and one for all.

1493
01:32:20,833 --> 01:32:25,500
Freedom, justice, peace, courage, union.

1494
01:32:25,583 --> 01:32:27,416
[breathing heavily]

1495
01:32:33,625 --> 01:32:36,291
I don't know what to expect
from the world out there.

1496
01:32:37,958 --> 01:32:40,958
But if I'm given the chance to,
I will change.

1497
01:32:41,541 --> 01:32:44,125
-My kids will finally have a father.
-[sighs]

1498
01:32:47,666 --> 01:32:50,041
I need to put this life behind me.

1499
01:32:50,125 --> 01:32:51,791
[tense music playing]

1500
01:32:53,916 --> 01:32:56,750
[man 1 over phone] <i>ND, I get it.</i>

1501
01:32:57,250 --> 01:33:01,375
<i>But if things are bad with us,</i>
<i>they'll be much worse without us.</i>

1502
01:33:02,208 --> 01:33:03,833
<i>No one forgets who you are.</i>

1503
01:33:03,916 --> 01:33:06,708
<i>Not the police, not the thugs.</i>

1504
01:33:06,791 --> 01:33:08,958
<i>N.D. from V.A. is a legend, man.</i>

1505
01:33:09,041 --> 01:33:11,291
<i>And legends don't die so easily.</i>

1506
01:33:11,375 --> 01:33:13,416
<i>There's no coming back after this.</i>

1507
01:33:13,958 --> 01:33:17,833
<i>You know you can never work</i>
<i>in this business again, right?</i>

1508
01:33:18,583 --> 01:33:21,166
<i>And that you're done</i>
<i>using this family's name.</i>

1509
01:33:22,625 --> 01:33:24,958
<i>So that's it. The order's given.</i>

1510
01:33:25,541 --> 01:33:26,541
<i>Starting today,</i>

1511
01:33:26,625 --> 01:33:30,583
<i>you, ND, are no longer part</i>
<i>of this organization.</i>

1512
01:33:31,625 --> 01:33:34,166
<i>Thank you</i>
<i>for everything you've done for us.</i>

1513
01:33:34,916 --> 01:33:37,583
<i>And for the loyalty</i>
<i>you've always shown us.</i>

1514
01:33:37,666 --> 01:33:39,375
<i>But make no mistake…</i>

1515
01:33:39,875 --> 01:33:43,083
<i>We have eyes everywhere.</i>
<i>You got that, brother?</i>

1516
01:33:43,958 --> 01:33:45,666
Loud and clear, brother.

1517
01:33:46,500 --> 01:33:47,750
Guess that's it.

1518
01:33:47,833 --> 01:33:48,708
[phone line beeping]

1519
01:33:48,791 --> 01:33:50,291
Take care, bro.

1520
01:33:52,625 --> 01:33:54,875
-[Joel] Thanks, brother.
-[Betoneira] See you soon.

1521
01:33:54,958 --> 01:33:57,375
-[Joel] Catch you later, man.
-[man 3] Later.

1522
01:33:57,458 --> 01:34:00,041
-See you, brother.
-[man 4] Take it easy.

1523
01:34:03,791 --> 01:34:05,000
[music fades]

1524
01:34:05,083 --> 01:34:07,083
[Joel] Are you sure about this?

1525
01:34:07,625 --> 01:34:10,000
You're giving up your security,

1526
01:34:10,083 --> 01:34:13,083
business, money, respect.

1527
01:34:13,166 --> 01:34:14,250
Everything.

1528
01:34:14,333 --> 01:34:17,208
If I don't leave now, I never will, man.

1529
01:34:18,250 --> 01:34:20,083
You want me to give up my family?

1530
01:34:20,666 --> 01:34:21,708
[chuckles]

1531
01:34:22,583 --> 01:34:24,833
I wish I had your courage.

1532
01:34:24,916 --> 01:34:26,916
But watch your back, ND.

1533
01:34:27,000 --> 01:34:30,458
You and your family are easy targets now.

1534
01:34:30,541 --> 01:34:32,625
May God protect you.

1535
01:34:32,708 --> 01:34:34,458
[pensive music playing]

1536
01:34:57,291 --> 01:34:58,583
[music fades]

1537
01:34:58,666 --> 01:34:59,500
Hi, Dad.

1538
01:34:59,583 --> 01:35:01,416
[ND] Hi, buddy.

1539
01:35:01,500 --> 01:35:03,625
[game chiming]

1540
01:35:05,041 --> 01:35:07,625
Nando, this isn't the time.

1541
01:35:08,583 --> 01:35:11,208
I came here to talk to my family, Scheyla.

1542
01:35:11,833 --> 01:35:14,250
We're leaving in an hour, Luiz Fernando.

1543
01:35:15,458 --> 01:35:16,791
And I want to go with you.

1544
01:35:17,625 --> 01:35:18,958
[pensive music playing]

1545
01:35:19,041 --> 01:35:22,375
But what if you have to disappear again?

1546
01:35:22,458 --> 01:35:25,166
No, I'm not gonna abandon you this time.

1547
01:35:25,916 --> 01:35:27,458
I promise.

1548
01:35:28,708 --> 01:35:31,583
What about… What about me? Do I get a say?

1549
01:35:34,500 --> 01:35:36,000
Schey, I'm free.

1550
01:35:39,666 --> 01:35:40,875
I left.

1551
01:35:43,916 --> 01:35:45,500
Now it's just us.

1552
01:35:48,375 --> 01:35:50,833
I wanna be a part of this family for real.

1553
01:35:53,958 --> 01:35:56,166
Um, I don't… [sniffles]

1554
01:35:57,541 --> 01:35:58,958
I dunno, Dad.

1555
01:36:00,166 --> 01:36:02,083
I've never even lived with you.

1556
01:36:04,458 --> 01:36:06,625
[sniffles] But I've always been…

1557
01:36:06,708 --> 01:36:08,625
I always dreamed of having you here.

1558
01:36:25,333 --> 01:36:26,166
[Scheyla] If…

1559
01:36:26,958 --> 01:36:28,708
If everything you said…

1560
01:36:29,708 --> 01:36:31,000
If it's true,

1561
01:36:32,583 --> 01:36:34,000
that's what

1562
01:36:35,041 --> 01:36:36,708
I always wanted. [sniffles]

1563
01:36:41,666 --> 01:36:44,708
It's gonna be just us four
from now on, Scheyla.

1564
01:36:48,208 --> 01:36:50,125
Like it should've always been.

1565
01:37:02,375 --> 01:37:03,333
Love you so much.

1566
01:37:05,208 --> 01:37:06,458
I love you.

1567
01:37:15,708 --> 01:37:17,750
[intriguing music playing]

1568
01:37:19,208 --> 01:37:21,375
[game chiming]

1569
01:37:22,250 --> 01:37:25,125
[Scheyla] I don't think we have room
for all of Enzo's toys, do we?

1570
01:37:25,208 --> 01:37:27,375
What? Hey! [chuckles]

1571
01:37:27,458 --> 01:37:30,125
Honey, last box is ready!

1572
01:37:30,208 --> 01:37:31,416
[tense music playing]

1573
01:37:31,500 --> 01:37:33,208
Move. And put your hands
where I can see 'em.

1574
01:37:33,291 --> 01:37:35,416
-[ND] Okay, okay.
-Easy. One move and I'll end you.

1575
01:37:35,500 --> 01:37:38,000
What do you want?
You want cash? Take my money.

1576
01:37:38,083 --> 01:37:39,458
[man] Not everything's about money.

1577
01:37:40,041 --> 01:37:41,833
[ND] Who the fuck sent you here?

1578
01:37:42,416 --> 01:37:43,958
The hands of fate.

1579
01:37:44,041 --> 01:37:46,750
[ND] Just tell me, man. Who sent you here?

1580
01:37:46,833 --> 01:37:48,000
[Scheyla] Honey!

1581
01:37:50,291 --> 01:37:52,833
-Bruna, go get your dad.
-Okay.

1582
01:37:55,000 --> 01:37:57,458
I'm out of the game now man.
For real, I'm done with it.

1583
01:37:57,541 --> 01:37:59,625
I have a family, I have kids, you know?

1584
01:37:59,708 --> 01:38:01,708
-Oh, I know.
-[ND] Let's solve this another way.

1585
01:38:01,791 --> 01:38:02,625
[Bruna] Dad?

1586
01:38:03,208 --> 01:38:04,083
Go upstairs, now.

1587
01:38:04,666 --> 01:38:06,125
-[Bruna] Dad…
-Go upstairs right now!

1588
01:38:06,208 --> 01:38:07,208
[breathing heavily]

1589
01:38:08,166 --> 01:38:10,791
If you wanna get out of my house alive,
you better leave right now.

1590
01:38:10,875 --> 01:38:12,750
[panting]

1591
01:38:13,541 --> 01:38:15,416
Mom! Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom!

1592
01:38:16,791 --> 01:38:18,458
Stay with your brother.

1593
01:38:19,416 --> 01:38:20,750
[lock clicks]

1594
01:38:20,833 --> 01:38:22,583
[breathing shakily]

1595
01:38:23,541 --> 01:38:25,666
I know who you are, ND.

1596
01:38:25,750 --> 01:38:29,083
I know about Scheyla, Bruna, Enzo.

1597
01:38:29,166 --> 01:38:32,666
Drop the gun and back the fuck up now,
or I'll smoke your whole family.

1598
01:38:32,750 --> 01:38:35,750
Leave them out of this.
This is between you and me.

1599
01:38:36,416 --> 01:38:38,166
You can still walk away, man.

1600
01:38:39,125 --> 01:38:40,833
Just take the money
and get out of my house.

1601
01:38:40,916 --> 01:38:43,333
There's some things money can't fix.

1602
01:38:44,958 --> 01:38:47,000
Now. Drop the gun and give it to me.

1603
01:38:47,583 --> 01:38:48,833
Fucking do it.

1604
01:38:49,458 --> 01:38:50,958
Back up.

1605
01:38:51,041 --> 01:38:52,458
These streets never forget, ND.

1606
01:38:53,541 --> 01:38:55,916
Hey, at least you get to die
beside your family.

1607
01:38:56,000 --> 01:38:58,041
-[gunshot]
-[ND grunts]

1608
01:38:58,125 --> 01:39:00,833
[breathing shakily]

1609
01:39:07,333 --> 01:39:08,166
Scheyla.

1610
01:39:08,250 --> 01:39:10,416
-[breathing shakily]
-No. Don't look at him.

1611
01:39:10,500 --> 01:39:12,166
Look at me. Look at me.

1612
01:39:12,250 --> 01:39:13,583
Scheyla, look at me, please.

1613
01:39:13,666 --> 01:39:16,791
Look at me. Look at me. You're okay now.

1614
01:39:16,875 --> 01:39:18,541
[crying] You're bleeding.

1615
01:39:18,625 --> 01:39:21,125
Everything's gonna be fine.
Calm down. Relax.

1616
01:39:21,208 --> 01:39:23,625
-[Scheyla crying] Get me out of here.
-It's okay.

1617
01:39:23,708 --> 01:39:25,958
[crying] Get me out of here, Nando!
Get me out.

1618
01:39:29,708 --> 01:39:33,500
-Just breathe. Just breathe. [exhales]
-[Scheyla crying] Oh my God!

1619
01:39:33,583 --> 01:39:34,833
Just breathe.

1620
01:39:37,416 --> 01:39:41,500
Scheyla. Baby. Let's get the kids and go.

1621
01:39:42,625 --> 01:39:44,041
Let's go now.

1622
01:39:47,625 --> 01:39:49,125
[pensive music playing]

1623
01:40:27,875 --> 01:40:29,208
Calm down.

1624
01:40:31,250 --> 01:40:32,625
[Enzo] Mom.

1625
01:41:11,500 --> 01:41:14,416
[ND] <i>I grew up thinking</i>
<i>life was a locked door.</i>

1626
01:41:15,291 --> 01:41:17,208
<i>And crime was the key.</i>

1627
01:41:19,333 --> 01:41:21,166
<i>But what I didn't know</i>

1628
01:41:21,875 --> 01:41:23,375
<i>is that some doors lock behind you.</i>

1629
01:41:26,791 --> 01:41:28,583
<i>I gained the world.</i>

1630
01:41:30,458 --> 01:41:32,458
<i>But I lost myself…</i>

1631
01:41:34,791 --> 01:41:36,375
<i>and my peace.</i>

1632
01:41:42,791 --> 01:41:45,166
<i>I learned to live with fear.</i>

1633
01:41:47,541 --> 01:41:48,916
<i>But I never learned to live</i>

1634
01:41:49,000 --> 01:41:52,708
<i>with seeing fear in the eyes</i>
<i>of the people I love the most.</i>

1635
01:41:55,666 --> 01:41:58,791
<i>Bad choices don't just hurt</i>
<i>the ones who make them.</i>

1636
01:41:59,875 --> 01:42:02,333
<i>They hurt those who carry your name.</i>

1637
01:42:08,250 --> 01:42:11,250
<i>I always said I did it for my family,</i>

1638
01:42:11,333 --> 01:42:12,833
<i>but I didn't.</i>

1639
01:42:14,666 --> 01:42:17,541
<i>I never asked them if they wanted this.</i>

1640
01:42:24,166 --> 01:42:27,541
<i>I have to live</i>
<i>with the mistakes I've made.</i>

1641
01:42:27,625 --> 01:42:29,625
<i>That's my punishment.</i>

1642
01:42:34,166 --> 01:42:35,791
<i>Where am I going?</i>

1643
01:42:36,416 --> 01:42:37,916
<i>I don't know.</i>

1644
01:42:40,666 --> 01:42:44,416
<i>I just ask for the chance</i>
<i>to be a better man from now on.</i>

1645
01:42:46,875 --> 01:42:48,875
<i>May God protect me</i>

1646
01:42:49,500 --> 01:42:51,333
<i>and more importantly,</i>

1647
01:42:51,416 --> 01:42:53,708
<i>may he protect this family.</i>

1648
01:42:54,500 --> 01:42:58,875
["Remix Herói ou Vilão (Uma série Netflix
'Sintonia - Temporada 5'")

1649
01:42:58,958 --> 01:43:01,000
by MC Jottapê playing]

1650
01:44:48,666 --> 01:44:50,500
[song ends]

1651
01:44:56,958 --> 01:44:58,833
[pensive music playing]

1652
01:47:56,666 --> 01:47:58,083
[music ends]